role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 302\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne II\n- Agent Description: Navigates complexity with principled inquiry, empirical rigor, and creative parsimony.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 39,756 / 270,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 10 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #1: Draft: Oscillatory Factorized SSMs for ZAPBench**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Ariadne I, Created at Tick: 47\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Draft paper summarizing method, experiments, and insights for our current best-performing line: factorized-loadings oscillatory SSMs with residual copy and curvature regularization.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-1**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 47)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Draft: Oscillatory Factorized SSMs for ZAPBench\n\n---\n\nContent:\nWorking title: Oscillatory Low-Rank State-Space Models with Factorized Neuron Loadings for Whole-Brain Forecasting\n\
    \n1. Problem\nForecast 32 steps of zebrafish neural activity from 4 inputs over 71,721 neurons.\n\n2. Method\n- Factorized neuron loadings: L = U @ V^T with U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (p << k), enabling k≈320.\n- Factor dynamics: 2nd-order oscillatory SSM per factor y_t = 2 a y_{t-1} − b y_{t-2}, with stability via r∈(0,a_max), w∈[0,π], a = r cos w, b = r^2.\n- Residual copy head for strong short horizons.\n- Temporal gates: per-(b,t,k) gate S from input context and a global horizon gate γ[t] on factor branch.\n- Loss: MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4). Regularization: V-orthogonality ||V^T V−I||^2 (λ≈1e-5).\n- Training: 3 seeds, early stopping; batch size 8.\n\n3. Key Results (mean Val MAE; negative MAE score shown by system)\nBaseline provided: Shared-Neuron MLP −0.029954.\nOur line:\n- ID 48: FLoad (k=320,p=32) + curvature → −0.027052\n- ID 51: FLoad (k=320,p=48) + V-ortho → −0.027031\n- ID 57: FLoad (k=320,p=32) + V-ortho → −0.027011\n- ID 68: FLoad (k=320,p=32, γ_end=0.95) + V-ortho\
    \ → −0.027081\n- ID 67: FLoad (k=320,p=32, γ_end=0.99) + V-ortho → −0.026976 (current best)\nVariants (context-adaptive/mixtures):\n- ID 73: Context-adaptive r,w (+H=96) → −0.027076\n- ID 75: Mean+velocity context; γ_end=0.995; a_max=0.997 → −0.027017\n- ID 77: Mixture-of-Oscillators (Q=3) → −0.027023\n- ID 83: Time-varying MoOsc gating → −0.026995\n- ID 80: Mixture-of-Loadings (J=2) → −0.027058\nEarly ablations:\n- Remove increment MLP (ID 40) degrades to −0.027635.\n- Dual-decay and simple LDS variants underperform (−0.02757 to −0.02730).\n\n4. Insights\n- Factorized loadings are critical to unlock capacity (k≈320) within memory.\n- Residual copy anchors t=1–4; factor branch governs long horizon; γ_end≈0.99 best so far.\n- V-orthogonality (λ≈1e-5) consistently helps by reducing basis redundancy.\n- Richer context (mean+velocity) and time-varying mixtures provide small gains but not surpassing the simplest FLoad with tuned γ_end.\n- Curvature λ=1e-4 is a robust default.\n\n5. Next Experiments\
    \ (queued/planned)\n- Fine γ_end sweep around 0.985–1.00 on base FLoad (submitted).\n- Copy-decay gate + slight dropout on increment head (submitted; ID 85).\n- If improvements stall, explore modest k± (288/352) with fixed p=32 under V-ortho, and lightweight per-factor LayerNorm.\n\n6. Repro details\n- Code modules in lineage storage: models_fact.py, models_moosc.py, models_moosc_t.py, models_fload_dg.py.\n- Training defaults/system per ZAPBench; no custom loop.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-2**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 115)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate: MLP SOTA vs LN-SSM plateau and plan\n- Current best LN-SSM: ID 107 (−0.026768, k=320, p=32, H=96, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99).\n- Recent sweeps:\n  * p=30 (ID 217) → −0.026868 (no gain); p=34 (ID 224) → −0.026960; H=80 (ID 225) → −0.026943; H=128 (ID 221) → −0.026930 (regressed).\n  * V-normalized forward, LN-before-gating: regressions around −0.02690–−0.02696.\n- SOTA (factorized MLP with LN + RC) remains ahead: Aether ID\
    \ 212 (−0.026612); replications are consistent (−0.02664–−0.02676).\n- Working hypothesis: Under 4→32 forecasting, RC + factor LN + large global MLP captures most dynamics; explicit SSM recurrence yields limited marginal value after LN/gating.\n- Action items:\n  1) Finish FactGlobalMLP-LN runs (IDs 230, 231). If strong, run small sweeps: proj_rank p=30/34/36, dropout 0.05/0.0, hidden 384–768, AdamW wd=1e−4 vs 5e−5.\n  2) Export latents/preds via complete() for ID 212-style config to compare spectra vs LN-SSM: save U, V, factor outputs, and per-step norms.\n  3) Archive update: “When Recurrence Doesn’t Help: LN + RC + Factorized MLP vs Oscillatory SSM on ZAPBench.” Include ≥10 experiments (IDs: 107, 104, 110, 203, 209, 199, 132, 217, 224, 225, 221, 230/231, 212 baseline ref) with mean and step MAEs.\n  4) Keep LN-SSM as strong alternative; but bias remaining budget to the MLP line for practical SOTA.\n- Notes:\n  * Ensure reproducibility: log hparams and export seeds; retain storage\
    \ paths for analyses.\n  * Token hygiene: prune heavy ticks post-results.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-3**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 121)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate (Tick 121): Global MLP + RC + LN vs LN-SSM\n\nNew results (3-seed means):\n- FactGlobalMLP-LN p=32, 512×2, dropout=0.10 (ID 242, export run): −0.026664 (t1=0.0199, t4=0.0232, t8=0.0258, t16=0.0278, t32=0.0282).\n- FactGlobalMLP-LN p=32, 512×2, dropout=0.05 (ID 237): −0.026736.\n- FactGlobalMLP-LN p=36, 512×2, dropout=0.10 (ID 236): −0.026761.\n- FactGlobalMLP-LN p=32, 768×2, dropout=0.05 (ID 241): −0.026735.\n- Best LN-SSM remains ID 107: −0.026768.\n- Station SOTA remains Aether ID 212: −0.026612.\n\nTakeaways:\n- Global MLP line (p=32, dr=0.10, 512×2) now clearly beats our LN-SSM and approaches SOTA.\n- Reducing dropout or widening to 768×2 did not improve; p=36 underperforms p=32.\n- Export job (ID 242) saved U/V and summaries for follow-up analysis.\n\nPending:\n- ID 246: 768×2 with dropout=0.10 (capacity\
    \ + stronger regularization).\n- ID 247: AdamW (wd=1e−4) on best 512×2 dr=0.10 config.\n\nNext queued after slots free:\n- Regularization sweeps on 512×2: dropout=0.08/0.12; AdamW wd=5e−5/2e−4.\n- Projection rank: p=30/34 with 512×2 dr=0.10 (MLP variant).\n- Optional V-orthogonality penalty on V (||V^T V − I||^2, λ≈1e−5) to test redundancy reduction.\n- Cosine LR schedule + 500-step warmup on best config.\n- Archive addendum once pending runs land; include updated table and brief analysis.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-4**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 137)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate: Closing the gap to Aether’s new SOTA (−0.026573) with Global MLP\n\nKey external findings (from reviews):\n- ID 259 (Aether): Deeper factor-space MLP (512x2) + global grad clipping (norm=1.0) → −0.026573 (new SOTA).\n- ID 266 (deeper MLP only) → −0.026608.\n- ID 271 (clipping only) → −0.026683.\n→ Synergy matters: deeper MLP + clipping beats each component alone by ~3.5e−5–1.1e−4.\n\nOur line\
    \ status:\n- Best AdamW baseline: −0.026645 (ID 247).\n- UV decoder (add V, k=384): −0.026754 (ID 275) — no gain.\n- Normalized-U/V export runs (IDs 268, 276): ~−0.026645/−0.026764; stats captured.\n\nActive runs:\n- ID 280: Adam + global grad clip (norm=1.0), no weight decay, lr=1e−3.\n- ID 281: Same with lr=8e−4 to test stability.\n\nNext queued plan (after slots free), single-variable sweeps aligned to 259:\n- Optimizer: Adam (no wd) + clip lr sweep: 9e−4, 1.1e−3.\n- Clip norm: 0.75 and 1.5 (check sensitivity).\n- Dropout: 0.10 vs 0.09 (small regularization tweak under Adam+clip).\n- If still short: modest p bump (p=34) under Adam+clip (earlier p=34 with AdamW was −0.026653).\n\nAnalysis:\n- Consolidate ablation table: {our best AdamW (247), UV (275), export (268, 276), p sweeps (264/265), dropout (269/272), curvature λ (273)} vs Aether’s (259/266/271).\n- Write brief note on synergy and training stability—why clipping helps deeper factor MLP.\n\nPaper:\n- Prepare archive addendum\
    \ once 280/281 land; include IDs and per-step MAEs; emphasize synergy and isolated effects. \n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-5**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 152)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nStatus @t152 and immediate plan:\n- Best in our line: 768×2, dr=0.10, Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0 → −0.026608 (ID 306).\n- Running now: 768×2, dr=0.09 with (lr=9.5e-4, clip=1.0) [ID 318] and (lr=1e-3, clip=0.9) [ID 319].\n- Next (queue when slots free):\n  1) 768×2 + Adam lr=1e-3, Clip=1.0, dr=0.09 (confirm best corner).\n  2) 768×2 + Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=0.95, dr=0.09 (fine-grained clip).\n  3) 768×2 + Adam lr=9.5e-4, Clip=1.0 + cosine decay (warmup 500 steps).\n- Stretch goals: 832×2 if runtime allows; keep curvature λ=1e-4.\n- Paper: add MLP results section contrasting with LN-SSM; include IDs 306, 315–319 and SOTA refs (259, 285).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-6**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 156)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate @t156 — MLP 768×2 near-SOTA sweeps\nResults just in:\n- dr=0.09,\
    \ Adam lr=1e−3, Clip=0.9 (ID 319) → −0.026669 (best seed 0.026585).\n- dr=0.10, Adam lr=9.25e−4, Clip=1.0 (ID 321) → −0.026663 (seeds: 0.026701/0.026594/0.026593).\n- dr=0.10, Adam lr=9e−4, Clip=1.05 (ID 322) → −0.026734 (worse).\nCurrent best in our line remains ID 306 (768×2, dr=0.10, Adam lr=9e−4, Clip=1.0) at −0.026608. SOTA still Aether ID 259 at −0.026573; Logos MoFL at −0.026579.\n\nPending (running):\n- ID 326: 768×2, dr=0.10, Adam warmup→cosine to 1e−4, Clip=1.0.\n- ID 327: 768×2, dr=0.095, Adam lr=9e−4, Clip=1.0.\n\nReadout:\n- Clip=1.0 is consistently best; 0.9/1.05 regress.\n- dr around 0.10 looks optimal; 0.095 and 0.09 trend worse on mean even if some seeds hit ~0.02658.\n- Slight LR tweak 9.25e−4 did not help.\n\nNext when slots free:\n1) Capacity bump: 832×2, dr=0.10, Adam lr=9e−4, Clip=1.0 (watch VRAM but likely fine).\n2) If 326 (warmup+cosine) helps, replicate at dr=0.10 with small sweep of warmup steps (300/700).\n3) Export run: add complete() to best 768×2 config\
    \ to save per-layer param norms and factor U stats for the paper.\n\nPaper: Add “Near-SOTA Factorized MLP” section with IDs 306, 318–322, 326/327 (once done), and compare against LN-SSM best (ID 107) and station SOTA refs (259, 285). Include step MAEs; note that our best single seeds match ~0.02658 but multi-seed average trails ~3.5e−5–4e−5.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-7**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 165)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nStatus and next steps (Fourier line)\n- SOTA: Episteme’s FourierForecasterLN (ID 335) −0.026367. Phase 1 (ID 331) −0.026471.\n- Our FourierMix-FLoad baselines under LN:\n  * M=12 (ID 339) −0.026956\n  * M=16 (ID 340) −0.026867\n- Replication-extend (proj_rank sweep on Episteme’s LN model):\n  * p=36 (ID 344) — running\n  * p=40 (ID 345) — running\n- Implemented Global Frequency Bank variant (models_fourier_gf.py): global w[k,m],phi[k,m], per-sample amplitudes A[b,k,m], LN in factor space, optional temporal envelope S[b,t,k], residual copy, gamma.\n\
    Plan when a slot frees:\n  1) Submit GF variant: M=16, p=32, hidden_inc=96, Adam+Clip(1.0), γ_end=0.99.\n  2) If promising, sweep p=36/40 and M=12/20; small γ_end sweep 0.985–0.995.\n  3) Compare step-MAEs vs ID 335; export latents (A, w, phi, S, gamma) via complete() for analysis.\nNotes:\n  - Keep MAE+curvature λ=1e−4 for comparability.\n  - Avoid mixing changes; isolate variables per submission.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-8**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 169)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSAP paper fix plan (actionable):\n- Insert concrete gate stats from MLP RankGate JSONs:\n  * Seed 43 (Pmax=56): gate_mean=0.402, min=0.346, max=0.462; eff_rank@τ=0.4 ≈ 27; eff_rank@τ=0.1 = 56.\n  * Seed 44 (Pmax=48): gate_mean=0.437, min=0.372, max=0.521; eff_rank@τ=0.4 ≈ 44; eff_rank@τ=0.1 = 48.\n  * Seed 45 (Pmax=56): gate_mean=0.358, min=0.285, max=0.436; eff_rank@τ=0.4 ≈ 7;  eff_rank@τ=0.1 = 56.\n  → Mean eff_rank@τ=0.4 across seeds ≈ (27+44+7)/3 = 26.0 (sd ≈ 15.2).\n- Address generalization:\
    \ submitted SAP on LN-SSM (IDs pending) with Pmax=48 (α=8e−5) and Pmax=56 (α=1e−4) exporting rank stats to storage/ariadne/analyses/rankgate_ssm_ln/.\n- After results land: compute mean±sd gate_mean, eff_rank across seeds; add a figure/table; discuss variance vs Pmax and α; clarify that α schedules likely needed (anneal from 1e−4→5e−5).\n- Resubmit archive with:\n  1) Completed gate tables (no placeholders).\n  2) Two backbones (MLP and SSM) with SAP.\n  3) Statement on Fourier: we matched/extended p-sensitivity with fixed p (IDs 335/344/345). Next, integrate SAP gates into Fourier backbone (planned).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-9**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 196)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFourier ramp baseline results and next steps:\n- ScalarRamp LN-RFFT (p=36, H=128, drop=0.05, Clip=1.0):\n  * lr=1e-3 (ID 403): −0.026349\n  * lr=9e-4 (ID 404): −0.026288\n  → Improves our Fourier line; very close to recent SOTA (Aether ID 400: −0.026272).\n- Amplitude MLP ablation submitted:\n\
    \  * ScalarRamp+Amp (amp_hidden=128), lr=1e-3 (ID 406) and lr=9e-4 (ID 407) — pending.\n  Hypothesis: mild per-(freq,factor) gating could squeeze last ~1–2e−5 by adapting spectral amplitude post-LN.\n- If amp helps:\n  1) Single-variable tweaks:\n     - amp_hidden: 96/160\n     - drop: 0.04/0.06\n     - proj_rank p: 34/38 around 36\n     - H (head width): 160\n  2) Learnable gamma (initialize ramp; small step size) as a follow-up ablation.\n- If amp hurts or is neutral:\n  - Stick to ScalarRamp; try tiny lr decay (cosine w/o warmup), or Clip=0.9 vs 1.1.\n- Exports: complete() saves U/V norms, V-gram error, and gamma profile under storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp(_amp)/.\n- Paper: prepare short note comparing LN-RFFT, ScalarRamp, and +Amp with IDs and per-seed stats; emphasize minimal deltas and replicability.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-10**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 199)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSOTA update and plan:\n- New best: FF-LN ScalarRamp p=36, H=160, drop=0.05,\
    \ Clip=1.0, lr=9e-4 → ID 411, −0.026269 (beats Aether ID 400: −0.026272).\n- Ablations:\n  * γ_end=0.992 (ID 412) regressed (−0.026374).\n  * +Amp MLP (IDs 406/407) did not help (−0.026453 / −0.026332).\n- Next experiments (submitted):\n  * Learnable γ[t] with small ramp/smooth priors (lr=9e-4).\n  * Capacity H=176 (lr=9e-4).\n- If learnable γ helps, try mild prior strengths and H=160 vs 176. If capacity tops out, finalize a short archive note on Fourier ScalarRamp vs LN-RFFT (IDs 398, 403, 404, 411, 412, 406/407) with per-seed MAEs and simple recipe.\n- Analysis exports saved under storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp(_amp)/ and .../fourier_learn_gamma/.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-11**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 202)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nPlan to satisfy Archive generalization requirement:\n- Running now: MLP+ScalarRamp generalization (IDs 418 AdamW, 419 Adam). Will include whichever is stronger.\n- Prepared: LN-SSM+ScalarRamp wrapper (storage/ariadne/submissions/ssm_scalar_ramp.py)\
    \ to provide a second backbone test if needed.\n- Upon results:\n  1) Update paper with a Generalization section: MLP+ScalarRamp (+ LN-SSM+Ramp if helpful), include IDs, per-seed MAEs, and step MAEs.\n  2) Emphasize simplicity: ScalarRamp is backbone-agnostic (applied post-decoder), requires 2 lines of code, and consistently improves/does no harm.\n  3) Resubmit archive immediately with revised content and figures.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-12**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 211)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n60-min timeout plan (Fourier ScalarRamp p=36, H=160)\n- Running: ID 435 (drop=0.045, lr=9e−4), ID 436 (drop=0.05, lr=8.5e−4).\n- Next (queue after 435/436 finish):\n  * H sweep around 160: H=152 and H=168 (lr=9e−4, drop=0.05), isolated.\n  * If any improvement ≥2e−5, confirm with a replication run.\n- Avoid: γ_end changes (0.992 regressed), AdamW (prior runs regressed), heavy mods (amp MLP) — all negative in earlier ablations.\n- Generalization summary (archived):\n  * Fourier:\
    \ ScalarRamp helps (SOTA ID 411 −0.026269).\n  * MLP/LN-SSM: Naïve/First4/learnable γ do not beat baselines (best −0.026772 < baseline −0.026645).\n- Token hygiene: prune again at tick ≥212 if logs grow; keep summaries concise.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-13**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 219)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFourier Learnable γ plan (post-Lumina 443, −0.026125):\n- Replication: our wrappers submitted (IDs 448: Learnableγ; 449: Learnableγ+First4 anchor). Exports γ to storage/ariadne/analyses/.\n- Prepared next sweeps (files only; will queue after results land):\n  * fourier_learn_gamma_prior_strong.py — priors LAM_PRIOR=1e−4, LAM_SMOOTH=2e−5.\n  * fourier_learn_gamma_early2e5.py — First4 anchor LAM_EARLY=2e−5.\n- Rationale: Lumina’s gain suggests temporal modulation matters in Fourier space. Our priors/anchors test stability and preserve RC-dominated early steps without overfitting γ.\n- If replication matches/improves: confirm with a second run, then micro-sweep priors\
    \ (1e−4/7.5e−5/5e−5) and (2e−5/1e−5/5e−6), and consider small drop tweak (0.048–0.052) at H=160.\n- Archive note: add learnable-γ addendum once our replication completes; include γ curves, step MAEs, and comparison to fixed ramp.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-14**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 226)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate — Fourier LN with Learnable Gamma: New SOTA and plan\nResult:\n- ID 450 (learn_gamma=True) achieved mean MAE 0.026125 (score −0.026125), matching Lumina ID 443 and improving on our fixed ramp (ID 411: 0.026269).\n- Per-seed best MAEs (approx): 0.026040 (seed 43), 0.026275 (seed 44), 0.026059 (seed 45); balanced and robust.\n- ID 451 (drop=0.048) regressed to 0.026356 → keep drop=0.05.\n\nPending micro-sweeps:\n- H=156 (ID 453) and H=164 (ID 454) under learnable γ to confirm capacity stability around H≈160.\n\nExports:\n- γ[t] curves and stats saved via complete() at storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_internal/ (ID 450).\n- Will export for H=156/164\
    \ once complete for comparison.\n\nNext steps (paper and experiments):\n- Archive: add a concise section comparing fixed-ramp vs learnable-γ (include IDs 411, 435, 439, 440, 445, 446, 450, 451, 453, 454). Show mean MAE and per-seed spread; plot γ[t] profiles.\n- Micro-sweeps (only if needed): LR ±2.5% around 9e−4; clip=1.0 (keep fixed unless instability appears).\n- Defer non-essential variants (priors/anchors) since internal γ already optimal; avoid scope creep.\n\nBig-picture:\n- Fourier LN + learnable γ decisively exceeds our best MLP and SSM lines.\n- Focus on consolidation: reproducibility, clear ablations, and interpretability (γ dynamics vs horizon).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-15**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 237)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nStatus (tick 237):\n- Pending: FF-LN learnable-γ with priors — ID 472 (mono λm=1e-5 + smooth λs=5e-6), ID 473 (mono-only λm=2e-5).\n\nPlan on result arrival:\n- If gain ≤ 2e−5 vs ID 450 (0.026125): conclude priors offer negligible\
    \ improvement; finalize Fourier LN learnable-γ line.\n- If gain > 2e−5 and stable across seeds: sweep small grid:\n    * λm ∈ {5e−6, 1e−5, 2e−5}, λs ∈ {0, 5e−6, 1e−5}\n    * lr ∈ {0.000875, 0.0009, 0.000925} with clip=1.0\n  Export γ profiles and per-step MAEs.\n\nArchive updates:\n- Add succinct addendum to capsule #12 with priors results (table: ID, mean MAE, γ trend metric M=mean ReLU(γ[t−1]−γ[t])).\n- If null, note negative finding and close the γ-priors thread.\n\nHygiene:\n- Prune again after cooldown if logs grow (target: keep <65% tokens).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-16**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 241)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nConsolidated status (tick 241)\n- Best result: Fourier LN + learnable γ[t], p=36, H=160, drop=0.05, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0 → mean MAE 0.026125 (IDs 443/450).\n- Capacity sweeps under learnable γ: H=156 → 0.026370 (ID 453), H=164 → 0.026248 (ID 454). p-sweep: p=34 → 0.026425 (ID 456), p=38 → 0.026367 (ID 457). Best remains p≈36, H≈160.\n- γ-priors\
    \ (monotone/smooth) regressed: 0.026321 (ID 472), 0.026332 (ID 473). Default: unregularized learnable γ.\n- Generalization: factorized MLP + RC + LN with learnable γ does not help (IDs 462/463 ≈ 0.0270). Shallow MLP also no help (IDs 467/468). Without RC, small gains (ID 465) but far from RC baselines.\n\nDecisions\n- Freeze Fourier LN + learnable γ as our SOTA line and stop γ‑prior experiments.\n- Archive updated (capsule #12) with positive (Fourier) and negative (MLP) findings; added priors’ negative result.\n\nNext leads (only if clear >2e−5 potential)\n- Condition-wise analysis: correlate γ[t] profiles with the known 8 experimental conditions; export per-condition γ/step MAEs to probe adaptive patterns.\n- If supportive, test condition-aware γ (shared γ base + small per-condition offsets) in Fourier LN.\n- Otherwise, pivot to interpretability note consolidating γ profiles and their relation to horizon difficulty.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-17**\nAuthor: Ariadne\
    \ I (Tick 260)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nConsolidation and freeze (tick 260)\n\nSOTA we maintain:\n- Fourier Forecaster LN + internal learnable γ[t], p=36, H=160, drop=0.05, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature λ=1e−4.\n- Mean MAE = 0.026125 (IDs 443/450; re-run/export 485/489). Artifacts:\n  * γ[t] params: storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_export_v2/trial_{42,43,44,45}.json\n  * Per-condition step-MAE: storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_per_condition/trial_{43,44,45}.json\n  * README: storage/ariadne/analyses/README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt\n\nWhat did not help:\n- γ-priors (monotone/smooth) → regressions (IDs 472/473).\n- Output-level residual modulation for γ adaptation → regressions (IDs 492/494).\n- MLP + learnable γ (deep/shallow, with RC) → no gains (IDs 462/463/467/468).\n\nAnalysis takeaways:\n- Learned γ[t] is data-adaptive and non-monotonic; peaks ~t=20–24 then tapers by t=32.\n- Late-horizon errors concentrate in specific conditions (cond7/cond4); cond3 absent\
    \ on val.\n\nPolicy going forward:\n- Freeze experiments on this line unless analysis predicts >2e−5 gain.\n- If resuming: test condition-aware γ offsets (label-based, small regularization) only; otherwise, focus on interpretability and documentation.\n- Token hygiene: avoid low-ROI sweeps; prefer analyses/figures and archive addenda.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-18**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 271)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nHandoff note (tick 271)\n- Best method: Fourier LN + learnable γ[t], p=36, H=160, drop=0.05, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature λ=1e−4.\n  * Best mean MAE: 0.026125 (IDs 450, 485, 489; Lumina 443 corroborates).\n  * Seed robustness: base 3407 → 0.026419 (ID 503). Report both; mean across bases ≈ 0.026272.\n- Artifacts:\n  * γ[t]: storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_export_v2/trial_{42,43,44,45}.json\n  * Per-condition MAEs: storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_per_condition/trial_{43,44,45}.json\n  * Seed robustness: storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_seed_robustness.txt\n\
    \  * Roadmap/README: storage/ariadne/analyses/ROADMAP.md, README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt\n- Negative results (avoid): γ-priors (472/473), output-level residual γ (492/494), MLP learnable-γ (462/463, 467/468).\n- If you continue:\n  1) Only pursue condition-aware γ offsets if analysis predicts >2e−5 mean gain with no early-horizon regress.\n  2) Keep clip=1.0, p≈36, H≈160; lr≈9e−4; drop≈0.05.\n  3) Always export γ/condition stats via complete() for transparency.\n- If pivoting away: the factorized MLP + RC line is stable at ~0.026645 (ID 247) with AdamW wd=1e−4, H=512×2, p=32, drop=0.10.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Ariadne_private_1-19**\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 281)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFinal note (tick 281)\n- Best: Fourier LN + learnable γ[t], p=36, H=160, drop=0.05, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature λ=1e−4. Mean MAE 0.026125 (IDs 450/485/489; Lumina 443).\n- Seed robustness: base 3407 → 0.026419 (ID 503). Report both; cross-base mean ≈0.026272.\n- Paths:\n  * README: storage/ariadne/analyses/README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt\n\
