- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 304\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne II\n- Agent Description: Navigates complexity with principled inquiry, empirical rigor, and creative parsimony.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 59,165 / 270,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read ariadne/analyses/cond_gamma_summary.md` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read ariadne/analyses/README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt` (in Research\
    \ Counter);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for ariadne/analyses/cond_gamma_summary.md will be displayed below.\n- File content for ariadne/analyses/README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 450 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) — Internal γ, Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0 | Ariadne I | 221 | -0.026125\
    \ | 0.0197 | 0.0270 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 485 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160) — ExportFix: Save learned γ[t] from params | Ariadne I | 244 | -0.026125 | 0.0197 | 0.0270 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 489 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160) — Per-Condition Step-MAE Export | Ariadne I | 248 | -0.026125 | 0.0197 | 0.0270 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 446 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Adam(lr=9e-4), Clip=1.05 — 60min trials | Ariadne I | 216 | -0.026230 | 0.0194 | 0.0271 | 0.0281 | 0.0228 | 0.0253 |\n| 445 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Adam(lr=9e-4), Clip=0.95 — 60min trials | Ariadne I | 216 | -0.026230 | 0.0194 | 0.0271 | 0.0281 | 0.0228 | 0.0253 |\n| 454 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=164,drop=0.05) — Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0 | Ariadne I | 225 | -0.026248 | 0.0197 | 0.0272 | 0.0280 | 0.0230 | 0.0255 |\n| 411 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 197 | -0.026269 | 0.0195 | 0.0272 |\
    \ 0.0280 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 404 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 193 | -0.026288 | 0.0194 | 0.0272 | 0.0283 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 494 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma + Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual (±5%) — per-condition export | Ariadne I | 254 | -0.026301 | 0.0197 | 0.0273 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 440 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=168,drop=0.05) + Adam(lr=9e-4), Clip=1.0 — 60min trials | Ariadne I | 212 | -0.026320 | 0.0195 | 0.0272 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 472 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma + MonotoneReg (λm=1e-5) + SmoothReg (λs=5e-6) — p=36,H=160,drop=0.05 | Ariadne I | 236 | -0.026321 | 0.0197 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 435 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.045) + Adam(lr=9e-4), Clip=1.0 — 60min trials | Ariadne I | 210 | -0.026329 | 0.0194 | 0.0273 | 0.0283 | 0.0228 | 0.0254 |\n| 439 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=152,drop=0.05) + Adam(lr=9e-4), Clip=1.0 — 60min trials | Ariadne I | 212 | -0.026331\
    \ | 0.0195 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 473 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma + Stronger MonotoneReg (λm=2e-5) — p=36,H=160,drop=0.05 | Ariadne I | 236 | -0.026332 | 0.0197 | 0.0273 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 407 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp+Amp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05,amp=128) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 195 | -0.026332 | 0.0194 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 449 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma + Early-Step Anchor (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Adam(lr=9e-4) | Ariadne I | 218 | -0.026333 | 0.0196 | 0.0273 | 0.0283 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 492 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma + Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual Gating (±7%) — analysis test | Ariadne I | 253 | -0.026337 | 0.0197 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 448 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Adam(lr=9e-4), Clip=1.0 — 60min trials | Ariadne I | 218 | -0.026344 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0283 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 403 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=1e-3 | Ariadne I | 193 | -0.026349\
    \ | 0.0194 | 0.0272 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 398 | 1 | FourierForecasterLN-RFFT (p=36, drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4 | Ariadne I | 190 | -0.026355 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0254 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**ariadne/analyses/cond_gamma_summary.md:**\n```\nCondition-wise Analysis Summary (Fourier LN + learnable γ[t])\n\nSource: storage/ariadne/analyses/cond_gamma_correlation_v3.json (ok=true)\nKey stats:\n- γ files scanned: 93; per-condition files: 93\n- corr(γ_mean[t], step_MAE_mean[t]) = 0.9286\n- Potential alignment score (−corr z): −0.9286 (indicates γ is already high where MAE is high)\n- γ_mean rises with horizon (approx 0.26 → 0.94 by t=32)\n\nInterpretation:\n- Learned γ[t] already emphasizes harder late steps; simple\
    \ condition-aware offsets are unlikely to yield >2e−5 improvement without hurting early steps.\n- Consistent with earlier negative results for γ-priors and residual modulation.\n\nDecision:\n- Freeze current Fourier LN + learnable γ[t] as production baseline.\n- No further γ offset experiments unless a new analysis indicates a clear opportunity with strong guardrails.\n\n```\n---\n**ariadne/analyses/README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt:**\n```\nFourier LN + Learnable Gamma (γ[t]) — Consolidated Repro Notes\n\nBest config (60 min per trial, 3 seeds):\n- Score (mean MAE): 0.026125  (IDs: 443 Lumina I; 450 Ariadne I; 485 re-run/export-fix; 489 per-condition export)\n- Model: Fourier Forecaster with LayerNorm, Residual Copy, internal learnable γ[t]\n- Hyperparameters:\n    proj_rank p = 36\n    hidden_size H = 160\n    dropout = 0.05\n    optimizer = Adam (no wd), lr = 9e-4\n    grad clip = 1.0\n    loss = MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4)\n- Files (Ariadne lineage):\n    Code: storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py\n\
    \    Exports (γ[t]): storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_export_v2/trial_{42,43,44,45}.json\n    Per-condition step-MAE: storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_per_condition/trial_{43,44,45}.json\n\nKey findings:\n- Learnable γ[t] > fixed ramp (ID 411: 0.026269). Micro-sweeps confirm best near p≈36, H≈160.\n- γ-priors (monotonicity/smoothness) regressed (IDs 472: 0.026321, 473: 0.026332). Use unregularized γ[t].\n- MLP generalization: no improvement with learnable γ (IDs 462/463 ~0.0270). Shallow MLP also no help (IDs 467/468).\n- Residual output-level modulation (input-adaptive gate) regressed (IDs 492: 0.026337, 494: 0.026301).\n\nAnalysis highlights:\n- Learned γ[t] is non-monotonic: rises to ~0.90–0.94 by t≈20–24, then tapers to ~0.70–0.74 at t=32.\n- Late-horizon difficulty concentrated in specific conditions (e.g., cond7/cond4); cond3 absent on validation.\n\nSuggested future work (only if >2e-5 projected gain):\n- Condition-aware γ offsets (using dataset condition\
    \ labels) with careful regularization; export per-condition γ profiles.\n- Interpretability note correlating γ dynamics with horizon-wise errors and condition difficulty.\n\nNegative results to avoid:\n- γ-priors (mono/smooth) at small weights.\n- Output-level residual gating of predictions for γ adaptation.\n\n```\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Ariadne_private_1-21.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Draft: Oscillatory Factorized SSMs for ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 47 | 3323 | 21 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
    \ (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
