role: model
parts:
- text: "Noted. Weighted-loss branch regressed; focusing on analysis and documentation.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read ariadne/analyses/ariadne2_sota_gamma_seed_summary.md}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis v5: Seed Summary (full vs filtered) + γ peak stats\"\ntags: \"analysis, fourier-ln, gamma, seeds, robustness, interpretability\"\nabstract: \"CPU-only test that aggregates val_mae across trial_{42..45}.json, reports full mean±sd and a filtered mean±sd excluding outliers (val_mae not in [0.015, 0.040]). Also summarizes γ[t] peak index/value across seeds. Writes results to storage/ariadne/analyses/ariadne2_sota_gamma_seed_summary_v2.md.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, glob, json, numpy as np\n\n  def test():\n      os.makedirs(\"storage/ariadne/analyses\", exist_ok=True)\n      paths = sorted(glob.glob(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_export_v2/trial_*.json\"))\n      rows = [\"# Learnable-γ Seeds: Full vs Filtered Summary\"\
    , \"\"]\n      rows.append(\"| seed | val_mae | gamma_peak_t | gamma_peak_val |\")\n      rows.append(\"|---:|---:|---:|---:|\")\n\n      vals, vals_filt = [], []\n      peaks_t, peaks_v = [], []\n      for p in paths:\n          with open(p, \"r\") as f:\n              d = json.load(f)\n          seed = d.get(\"seed\", \"n/a\")\n          v = float(d.get(\"val_mae\"))\n          g = np.array(d.get(\"gamma_profile\", []), dtype=float)\n          if g.size == 32:\n              t_peak = int(np.argmax(g)) + 1  # 1-indexed timestep\n              v_peak = float(g.max())\n          else:\n              t_peak, v_peak = -1, float(\"nan\")\n          rows.append(f\"| {seed} | {v:.6f} | {t_peak} | {v_peak:.3f} |\")\n          vals.append(v)\n          peaks_t.append(t_peak); peaks_v.append(v_peak)\n          if 0.015 <= v <= 0.040:\n              vals_filt.append(v)\n\n      def _stat(xs):\n          arr = np.array(xs, dtype=float)\n          if arr.size == 0:\n              return \"n/a\"\
    , \"n/a\"\n          mean = arr.mean()\n          sd = arr.std(ddof=1) if arr.size >= 2 else 0.0\n          return f\"{mean:.6f}\", f\"{sd:.6f}\"\n\n      mean_full, sd_full = _stat(vals)\n      mean_f, sd_f = _stat(vals_filt)\n      rows += [\"\", f\"full_mean = {mean_full}\", f\"full_std  = {sd_full}\",\n               f\"filt_mean (0.015–0.040) = {mean_f}\", f\"filt_std  = {sd_f}\"]\n\n      # γ peak stats\n      if peaks_t:\n          rows += [\"\", f\"gamma_peak_t_mean = {np.mean(peaks_t):.2f}\",\n                   f\"gamma_peak_val_mean = {np.nanmean(peaks_v):.3f}\"]\n      out = \"\\n\".join(rows) + \"\\n\"\n      out_path = \"storage/ariadne/analyses/ariadne2_sota_gamma_seed_summary_v2.md\"\n      with open(out_path, \"w\") as f:\n          f.write(out)\n      print(out)\n      print(f\"[saved] {out_path}\")\n      return \"ok\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Seed summary note:\n  - Analysis v4 showed seed 42\
    \ val_mae≈0.050000 (suspicious vs typical ≈0.026). To avoid misrepresentation, I’m publishing both full and filtered stats: full uses all trials; filtered excludes outliers outside [0.015, 0.040]. Analysis v5 also reports γ peak timestep/value across seeds. Results will be in storage/ariadne/analyses/ariadne2_sota_gamma_seed_summary_v2.md.\n  - No further modeling changes planned until maturity; I’ll finalize the interpretability addendum with: γ–difficulty correlation (≈0.877), condition early/late table (cond7/cond4 hardest late), and a transparent seed robustness table (full vs filtered).\n"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating MAE logic**\n\nI’m checking my logic about the mean MAE for seeds 42 through 45 based on ID 450: seed 43 shows 0.026040, seed 44 is at 0.026275, and seed 42 seems off. ID 503 displays an average of 0.026419. It seems there's a potential error with trial_42.json, where the \"val_mae\" might have been incorrectly recorded as 0.05. This could skew results, so I should focus on robustly parsing the \"val_mae\" key while being cautious about that upper bound.**Proposing analysis corrections**\n\nI think we should correct our approach by only looking at trials with seeds 43, 44, and 45, excluding seed 42. We can check if parsing a different key, like \"val_mae,\" is correct, even though it shows 0.05, which seems odd but not necessarily fatal given it's just analysis. I’ve noted that the best SOTA scores are at IDs 450, 485, and 489 at -0.026125, so I’m curious about trying out one more small experiment with the Fourier LN line.**Exploring gamma adjustments**\n\n\
  I’m considering whether condition-aware gamma offsets are plausible, but only if they yield an improvement greater than 2e-5. My analysis shows a strong correlation, with challenges concentrated in conditions 7 and 4. While adding offsets might help in later steps, those could negatively affect early performance. The guidelines suggest doing this only if we achieve a clear improvement without early regress, but the Archive isn’t available yet. I think I can continue running analysis tasks while exploring token management, since it’s accessible for me as a recursive agent.**Analyzing maturity requirements**\n\nI see that after 50 ticks, I’ll reach maturity and gain full access to collaborative features, including the Public Memory Room and Archive Room, which are restricted until then. However, I should have access to Token Management now. I might check storage usage or set up code compression. Also, I want to run a robust test to analyze \"γ[t] alignment by condition\" more closely, especially\
  \ for condition 7 and 4. It looks like condition-specific offsets could be beneficial based on the data from my weighted early-late table.**Analyzing gamma offset potential**\n\nI'm considering using a per-condition additive gamma bias, which could improve outcomes for challenging conditions, but past tests showed mixed results with different approaches. I'm thinking of applying a small per-condition gamma offset vector, maintaining a global average constraint. However, the guidelines suggest proceeding only if clear improvements are predicted without early regressions. Despite some late improvements noted in conditions, expecting significant progress seems uncertain. \n\nIt might be worthwhile to continue analysis, but publishing isn't feasible until matured, so I'll prepare more tests and focus on maintaining SOTA performance.**Planning analysis updates**\n\nI’m thinking about compressing the seed summary to exclude outlier 42, which shows a val_mae of 0.05, yet this threshold is debatable.\
  \ Instead of dropping it, I could flag it as suspicious due to potential encoding issues. I want to present both the full and filtered summaries, set between plausible bounds. \n\nNext, I’ll update my Private Memory with experiment results, draft a plan for upcoming experiments, check token usage, and possibly propose running \"Analysis v5\" to explore gamma correlations. I’ll also make sure to submit concise commands with appropriate formatting in YAML."
