parts:
- text: "Submitting Idea 3 confirmation on the stronger fixed-ramp baseline (H=160), then logging a concise progress summary and updating the plan.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 3 confirm: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160) + Population-Mean Alignment (λ_pop=1e-3) + Curvature\"\ntags: \"baseline, fourier, scalar-ramp, population-mean, loss, curvature\"\nabstract: \"Confirm Idea 3 on a stronger fixed-ramp baseline: Fourier LN ScalarRamp with H=160 (learn_gamma=False), adding a horizon-wise population-mean alignment penalty λ_pop=1e−3 on top of MAE+curvature (λ=1e−4). Tests whether the larger H improves robustness of the observed gain.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, sys\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n    \
    \      'proj_rank': 36,      # p\n          'hidden_size': 160,   # H (confirmation)\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': False, # fixed scalar ramp baseline\n          'lambda_pop': 1e-3    # population-mean alignment strength\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_base_network(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lam_pop = hparams.get('lambda_pop', 1e-3)\n\n      # Primary MAE\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\n      # Temporal curvature penalty (second-difference L1 across time)\n      d2 = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curvature = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n\n      # Population-mean alignment per horizon\n      pred_mean_t = jnp.mean(predictions, axis=(0, 2))  # (32,)\n      true_mean_t = jnp.mean(targets,     axis=(0, 2))  # (32,)\n\
    \      mean_align = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(pred_mean_t - true_mean_t))\n\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curvature + lam_pop * mean_align\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/pop_mean_penalty\", exist_ok=True)\n          out = {\n              \"trial_number\": trial_data.get(\"trial_number\"),\n              \"seed\": trial_data.get(\"seed\"),\n              \"val_mae\": trial_data.get(\"val_mae\"),\n              \"hyperparameters\": trial_data.get(\"hyperparameters\"),\n              \"note\": \"ScalarRamp H=160 with population-mean alignment (lambda_pop=1e-3) + curvature (confirmation)\"\n          }\n          with open(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/pop_mean_penalty/confirm_H160_lambda_1e-3.json\", \"w\") as f:\n              json.dump(out,\
    \ f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/stagnation_protocol_progress.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Stagnation Protocol Progress (Ariadne II)\n  Baseline (ScalarRamp, p=36)\n  - H=128 (ID 565): mean MAE 0.026387 (score −0.026387)\n  - H=160 (ref ID 411): mean MAE 0.026269 (score −0.026269)\n\n  Idea 1 — Huber loss + curvature (λ=1e−4)\n  - H=128:\n    * δ=0.01 (ID 567): 0.026347  (gain ≈ +4.0e−5 vs repro)\n    * δ=0.02 (ID 569): 0.026389  (regressed)\n    * δ=0.03 (ID 570): 0.026358  (gain ≈ +2.9e−5)\n  - H=160:\n    * δ=0.01 (ID 576): 0.026253  (gain ≈ +1.6e−5 vs 0.026269; below 2e−5 threshold → marginal)\n  - Status: Accept on H=128 (δ=0.01). On H=160, effect is marginal.\n\n  Idea 2 — Variance-weighted horizon MAE (stop-grad), α=0.25\n  - H=128 (ID 574): 0.026397 (regressed vs baseline 0.026387)\n  - Status: Reject.\n\n  Idea 3 — Population-mean alignment penalty, λ_pop=1e−3\n\
    \  - H=128 (ID 579): 0.026316 (gain ≈ +7.1e−5 vs baseline; best among simple-baseline ideas)\n  - H=160: confirmation submitted (ID pending)\n  - Status: Promising on H=128; confirming on H=160.\n\n  Synthesis — Apply best loss to advanced backbone\n  - Learnable-γ (p=36, H=160) + Huber(δ=0.01): submitted (ID 580, running)\n\n  Notes\n  - Early steps (t1–t4) remained stable for Huber δ=0.01 and λ_pop=1e−3 on H=128.\n  - Variance-weighting was noisy and neutral/negative; no further α sweep planned to conserve budget.\n  - Next steps: (1) Await Idea 3 confirmation (H=160) and synthesis (ID 580). (2) If Idea 3 confirms at H=160 and/or transfers to learnable-γ, include in report; otherwise present as strong H=128-only finding. (3) Draft Archive note summarizing baseline, three ideas, and synthesis with IDs and mean±sd where available.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update:\n  - Idea 3 (λ_pop=1e−3) on H=128 achieved −0.026316\
    \ (best simple baseline so far, +7.1e−5 gain vs −0.026387). Confirmation on H=160 submitted.\n  - Idea 1 (Huber δ=0.01) is positive on H=128 but marginal on H=160 (−0.026253 vs −0.026269; +1.6e−5 < 2e−5 threshold). Synthesis on learnable-γ is running (ID 580).\n  - Idea 2 (variance-weight α=0.25) regressed; closed.\n  - Plan: finalize stagnation report with baseline repro, three ideas (isolated sweeps), and synthesis; accept Huber δ=0.01 (H=128) and λ_pop=1e−3 (H=128); report marginal/negative results transparently; include H=160 confirmations and learnable-γ synthesis outcomes once they land.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating improvements**


  I’m looking at the Huber improvement on H=160, which gives -0.026253 — that’s a slight gain of 1.6e-5, just under our detection threshold of 2e-5. Earlier, I noted that Idea 1 seemed positive, but the measurement doesn’t cross the threshold, so it’s marginal. With Idea 1, I previously accepted it at H=128, where it had a gain of 4.0e-5. Now, I want to test Idea 3 at H=160 and also try the learnable gamma with the population mean penalty. Idea 2, on the other hand, is a no-go at -0.026397.**Planning next steps**


  I’ve got some actions lined up. First, I need to write an analysis log summary. Then I’ll submit Idea 3 for confirmation at H=160 with a fixed ramp baseline and λ_pop set to 1e-3, but I’m considering testing alternate values like 2e-3 or 5e-3—just one at a time due to concurrency limits. Right now, only experiment ID 580 is running, so I can submit one more. I also want to write a draft for the "Stagnation Protocol Report" for archiving. It''s good to have this organized!**Organizing stagnation protocol actions**


  The stagnation protocol says to skip the literature review if it''s immature, but system tips suggest previewing it, although that’s not a requirement. I need to focus on specific actions: submitting the confirmation and writing a summary. I’ll draft the code for Idea 3 confirmation, using a similar compute_loss structure with the λ_pop parameter at H=160. I’ll also ensure the training loops remain unchanged. Afterward, I’ll document the completion in the specified JSON file and consider writing a YAML update regarding acceptance criteria, especially noting that Idea 1 is marginally below the threshold.**Finalizing assistant actions**


  Let’s organize the final steps. First, I’ll go to research and submit Idea 3 confirmation with the appropriate code. Then I need to write a summary update file named ''ariadne/analyses/stagnation_protocol_progress.md'', detailing the results and relevant numbers.


  I also have to check private memory and reply to capsule 2 with the update while being mindful of the concurrency limit, since only one confirmation can be added. I’ll compute the summary text carefully to avoid any errors, reviewing the baselines and improvements from each idea accordingly. Finally, I’ll code for the Idea 3 confirmation loss computation.**Preparing actions for completion**


  I need to make sure to properly title the document, add relevant tags, and draft an abstract. Once everything is ready, I’ll write "complete" to the JSON file. I’m also thinking about proposing to schedule Idea 3 with the learnable gamma after confirming, but I need to hold off for now since the concurrency limit will be reached with two evaluations (580 plus the new confirm). Once that’s clear, I''ll be ready to output everything efficiently!'
