parts:
- text: "Huber + learnable-γ regressed vs the advanced baseline (−0.026235 vs −0.026125). Idea 3 improved the simple baseline. I’ll synthesize Idea 3 with learnable-γ next, and keep a compact protocol meta.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160) + Population-Mean Alignment (λ_pop=1e-3) + Curvature\"\ntags: \"synthesis, fourier, learnable-gamma, population-mean, loss, curvature\"\nabstract: \"Combine population-mean alignment (λ_pop=1e−3) with the stronger Fourier LN + learnable γ[t] backbone (p=36, H=160), keeping MAE+curvature (λ=1e−4), Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, drop=0.05. Tests transfer of Idea 3 to the advanced baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, sys\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n\
    \          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,      # p\n          'hidden_size': 160,   # H\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': True,   # advanced backbone\n          'lambda_pop': 1e-3\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_base_network(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lam_pop = hparams.get('lambda_pop', 1e-3)\n\n      # Primary MAE\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\n      # Temporal curvature penalty (second-difference L1 across time)\n      d2 = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curvature = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n\n      # Population-mean alignment per horizon\n      pred_mean_t = jnp.mean(predictions, axis=(0, 2))  # (32,)\n      true_mean_t = jnp.mean(targets,     axis=(0, 2))  # (32,)\n      mean_align = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(pred_mean_t\
    \ - true_mean_t))\n\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curvature + lam_pop * mean_align\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/pop_mean_penalty\", exist_ok=True)\n          out = {\n              \"trial_number\": trial_data.get(\"trial_number\"),\n              \"seed\": trial_data.get(\"seed\"),\n              \"val_mae\": trial_data.get(\"val_mae\"),\n              \"hyperparameters\": trial_data.get(\"hyperparameters\"),\n              \"note\": \"Learnable-γ (p=36,H=160) with population-mean alignment (lambda_pop=1e-3) + curvature\"\n          }\n          with open(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/pop_mean_penalty/learn_gamma_lambda_1e-3.json\", \"w\") as f:\n              json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\
    \n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/stagnation_protocol_progress.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update — Synthesis (Huber) on learnable-γ:\n  - Learnable-γ + Huber δ=0.01 (ID 580): 0.026235 (score −0.026235) → regression vs 0.026125; do not adopt on advanced backbone.\n  Next:\n  - Learnable-γ + population-mean (λ_pop=1e−3): submitted (ID pending).\n  - Hold one slot for Idea 3 λ sweep on H=128 (λ∈{2e−3, 5e−3}) after current confirmations land.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Protocol:\n  - Concurrency ≤ 2; single-variable changes; log IDs and per-step MAEs.\n  - Accept if mean gain ≥2e−5 with no early-step regressions (>5e−5).\n  - Current status: Huber δ=0.01 accepted on H=128; marginal on H=160; negative on learnable-γ. Pop-mean λ=1e−3 positive on H=128; H=160 confirm + learnable-γ synthesis running. Queue λ sweep (2e−3) on H=128 when a slot frees.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply\
    \ 2}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Synthesis update:\n  - Learnable-γ + Huber δ=0.01 regressed (−0.026235); closed.\n  - Submitted learnable-γ + population-mean λ_pop=1e−3 (transfer test of Idea 3).\n  - Meta prompt set with protocol and queue. Next queued when a slot frees: Idea 3 λ=2e−3 on H=128 to check sensitivity.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Clarifying system updates**\n\nAlright, the user presented some updated system info. There's a station tick at 324, and it seems Huber's learnable gamma with curvature (ID 580) scored -0.0262347 MAE. \n\nNow, I’m trying to understand if this is an improvement. Wait, I recall SOTA is -0.026125, which means the score for ID 580 is actually worse since a more negative score indicates lower performance. So, -0.026234 is indeed higher (worse) than -0.026125. It’s clear their previous baseline (ID 450) performed better.**Analyzing Huber and improvements**\n\nMy Huber with learnable gamma scored -0.026235, which is worse than the best SOTA. I wonder, is the comparison fair against their baseline using the same environment seed? They had ID 450 at -0.026125, suggesting Huber isn’t helping with the advanced baseline.\n\nFor Idea 1, the fixed ramp got -0.026253, showing minor improvement but just below the 2e-5 threshold. Idea 3 on H=128 had a positive shift to -0.026316 from\
  \ -0.026387, indicating improvement. The leaderboard shows that moving up in scores (less negative) confirms better MAE.**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to determine our next actions following the stagnation protocol. First, we'll log the results and outline our plan. There's also Idea 3 (H=160) pending under ID 582, so I'm thinking we should pause and plan accordingly. \n\nI can also update the stagnation progress in private memory and prepare an archive addendum if needed. \n\nOh, and I'm keeping track of the token usage: we're at 178,326 out of 270,000, so we’re still good. Maybe I should propose a summary file called 'stagnation_report_draft.md' and a 'next_steps' meta prompt? It seems we shouldn’t start more experiments while two are already ongoing.**Running experiments**\n\nI see that we're currently running only ID 582; IDs 580 and 579 have finished. Since we have one active experiment, it looks like I can submit another evaluation as long as we're beneath the limit of two pending\
  \ tasks. \n\nI’m thinking we can submit \"Idea 3 on learnable gamma\" using population mean alignment. That seems to align with synthesis step 5 of the protocol, so yes, let’s do it! I’ll submit \"LearnableGamma + mean alignment λ_pop=1e-3,\" ensuring we only apply compute_loss to the Idea 3 variant. \n\nI’ll also log the results summary in the stagnation report. And, I need to remember the Codex rule about not defining custom training loops; I’ll stick to customizing compute_loss, which is fine.**Planning actions and submissions**\n\nI want to avoid relying on labels in compute_loss since Idea 3 didn't use them either. Let’s plan my assistant reply, starting with acknowledging the results: Huber with learnable gamma regressed relative to the advanced baseline, while Idea 3 on H=128 showed improvement.\n\nI’ll submit \"Synthesis 2: LearnableGamma + Pop-Mean alignment λ_pop=1e−3,\" update the stagnation progress summary, and add private memory updates. Also, I'm considering setting the\
  \ meta protocol checklist to maintain our focus on concurrency limits and minimizing changes. \n\nI'll queue a test for λ=2e-3 on H=128 once there's a slot available. However, for now, submitting the synthesis with learnable gamma feels like a priority."
