role: model
parts:
- text: "Proceeding with the λ sweep for Idea 3 on the simple baseline (H=128), then logging progress.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 3b: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128) + Population-Mean Alignment (λ_pop=2e-3) + Curvature\"\ntags: \"baseline, fourier, scalar-ramp, population-mean, loss, curvature\"\nabstract: \"Sensitivity test for Idea 3 on the simple ScalarRamp baseline: increase population-mean alignment to λ_pop=2e−3 on top of MAE+curvature (λ=1e−4). Config: p=36, H=128, drop=0.05, lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, learn_gamma=False.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, sys\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,      # p\n          'hidden_size': 128,   # H\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start':\
    \ 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': False, # fixed scalar ramp baseline\n          'lambda_pop': 2e-3    # sweep: stronger population-mean alignment\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_base_network(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      lam_pop = _define_hyperparameters().get('lambda_pop', 2e-3)\n\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      d2 = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curvature = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n\n      pred_mean_t = jnp.mean(predictions, axis=(0, 2))  # (32,)\n      true_mean_t = jnp.mean(targets,     axis=(0, 2))  # (32,)\n      mean_align = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(pred_mean_t - true_mean_t))\n\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curvature + lam_pop * mean_align\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n\
    \      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/pop_mean_penalty\", exist_ok=True)\n          out = {\n              \"trial_number\": trial_data.get(\"trial_number\"),\n              \"seed\": trial_data.get(\"seed\"),\n              \"val_mae\": trial_data.get(\"val_mae\"),\n              \"hyperparameters\": trial_data.get(\"hyperparameters\"),\n              \"note\": \"ScalarRamp H=128 with population-mean alignment (lambda_pop=2e-3) + curvature\"\n          }\n          with open(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/pop_mean_penalty/lambda_2e-3.json\", \"w\") as f:\n              json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/stagnation_protocol_progress.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update — Idea 3 confirmation and next sweep:\n  - H=160 confirm (λ_pop=1e−3, ID 582): 0.026293 → slight regression vs 0.026269\
    \ baseline; effect appears H=128-only.\n  - Synthesis Huber on learnable-γ regressed; synthesis pop-mean on learnable-γ running (ID 584).\n  - Queued λ_pop=2e−3 on H=128 to check sensitivity; will only proceed to 5e−3 if 2e−3 improves without early-step harm.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Protocol note:\n  - Idea 3 confirmed marginal/negative at H=160 (−0.026293), but positive on H=128 (−0.026316). Submitted H=128 λ_pop=2e−3 sweep. Learnable-γ + pop-mean is running (ID 584).\n  - Acceptance rule unchanged (≥2e−5 gain, no early-step regressions). If 2e−3 helps, replicate; else close Idea 3 with λ=1e−3@H=128 as the best simple-baseline finding.\n```"
