    ```\n`/execute_action{storage write ariadne/reports/stagnation_report_draft.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Stagnation Protocol I: Loss Probes and Minimal Calibration on ScalarRamp Baseline\n\n  Summary\n  - Baseline: Fourier LN ScalarRamp (p=36), H=128, MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4), lr=9e-4, clip=1.0, drop=0.05.\n  - Three loss ideas tested with single-variable changes and 3-seed means. Acceptance: ≥2e-5 improvement with no early-step regressions (>5e-5).\n  - Results on H=128:\n    * Huber(δ=0.01): −0.026347 (gain ~4.0e-5) — accepted.\n    * Pop-mean penalty (λ=1e-3): −0.026316 (gain ~7.1e-5) — accepted.\n    * Variance-weighted MAE (α=0.25): −0.026397 — rejected.\n  - Confirmations/synthesis:\n    * Huber δ=0.01 on H=160: −0.026253 (marginal).\n    * Pop-mean on H=160: −0.026293 (rejected).\n    * Transfer to learnable-γ (H=160): negative for both Huber and pop-mean.\n  - Minimal architecture test (running): 32-scalar horizon bias head on ScalarRamp (H=128/160).\n\n  Methods\n  - Kept training\
    \ system defaults; no custom loops. Three seeds per trial with early stopping.\n  - Logged early (t=1,4), mid (t=8,16), late (t=32) step MAEs; see analyses CSV at ariadne/analyses/summary_scalaramp_loss_arch.csv.\n\n  Experiments (selected)\n  - 565 Baseline (H=128): −0.026387; step MAEs: 0.0195, 0.0230, 0.0255, 0.0274, 0.0284.\n  - 567 Huber δ=0.01 (H=128): −0.026347; 0.0195, 0.0229, 0.0255, 0.0273, 0.0282.\n  - 579 Pop-mean λ=1e-3 (H=128): −0.026316; 0.0195, 0.0229, 0.0255, 0.0273, 0.0281.\n  - 574 Variance-weight α=0.25 (H=128): −0.026397; rejected.\n  - 576 Huber δ=0.01 (H=160): −0.026253; marginal vs H=160 reference (−0.026269).\n  - 582 Pop-mean λ=1e-3 (H=160): −0.026293; rejected.\n  - 580 Learnable-γ + Huber δ=0.01: −0.026235; rejected.\n  - 584 Learnable-γ + Pop-mean λ=1e-3: −0.026455; rejected.\n\n  Insights\n  - On a simple ScalarRamp baseline, robust loss and a small global-mean penalty yield small, consistent gains; effects do not scale with capacity (H=160) and do not transfer\
    \ to learnable-γ, suggesting their benefit addresses minor biases smoothed out by stronger temporal weighting capacity.\n  - Variance-weighting by dispersion did not help, indicating batch-level horizon difficulty adaptation is not a missing ingredient at this capacity.\n\n  Next Steps\n  - Await results from minimal horizon-bias calibration head (IDs 592, 593). If positive on H=128 and confirmed on H=160, test transfer to learnable-γ; else close architecture probe.\n  - Prepare a negative/qualified-results note with full tables and per-seed stats once the head results finish.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiment details**\n\nI should clearly record the plan. While runs 592 and 593 are executing, I need to gather per-step MAE curves and early/late aggregates from previous relevant runs, like the baselines and Huber with different parameters. I'll also collect logs using the execute action function when needed.\n\nI need to add a code or storage writer to keep a small CSV summary, updating it in lineage storage. After I see results from the bias head, I'll plan the next steps with minimal architecture changes.**Evaluating next steps**\n\nI've already launched the H=160 confirmation. If it shows improvement, I might also consider synthesizing to SOTA with learnable-γ, but I can't queue anything right now since concurrency is limited.\n\nI could attempt a mild sweep on bias_scale to test effect sizes after the results come in. Meanwhile, efficiency can be managed by pruning tokens but there’s a cooldown period.\n\nI can also use storage actions, like checking\
  \ usage or saving code modules. It's possible to visit the Reflection Chamber again, although it’s not necessary. The Public Memory Room isn't currently available either, as it requires maturity.**Gathering evaluation logs**\n\nIt’s not necessary to submit new actions right now since we have no concurrency left; we already submitted two concurrently. I want to gather logs for the finished evaluations that haven’t been reviewed yet, specifically for runs 588 and 582, as well as 570 and 569 for Huber sweeps. I’ve previously reviewed 580 and 584, but we can fetch details on the others.\n\nAdditionally, I’ll compile a summary CSV that combines mean MAE scores and early/late step values, but I’ll need to gather those values first.**Compiling evaluation data**\n\nI see that we already have some information in the 'Submitted Evaluations' table for Val_MAE_1, 4, 8, 16, 32, and the final \"Score\" with negative MAE. However, for per-step curves, it seems the reviews include epoch logs but lack\
  \ step-wise MAE at each step.\n\nI can rely on the table for creating a CSV summary, but I still need to list the values correctly. Instead of manually parsing, it might be better to use the 'review evaluation_id' command to get full logs and code, although I’m unsure if the step-wise MAEs are included. The existing 5 time steps in the table should be sufficient for a small summary.**Planning evaluations and reports**\n\nI can run the 'preview all' command to get details on submissions, but it’s more efficient to focus on our specific evaluations. I’ll review the logs for runs 588, 582, 570, 569, and 574.\n\nNext, I need to write a summary file in 'storage/ariadne/analyses' that includes accepted/rejected decisions and reasons. I’ll also prepare a draft for the stagnation report. I can compile a CSV with evaluation data and monitor concurrency while waiting for results from Idea 4. After those are ready, I can propose potential next steps.**Finalizing decisions and reports**\n\nI've decided\
  \ to mark δ=0.01 as accepted since it meets the threshold, while δ=0.03 shows improvements but isn't chosen as the preferred setting. I’ll also categorize several evaluations, noting which ones were rejected or accepted. \n\nIt’s time to draft the 'stagnation_report_draft.md' with a clear structure: Intro, Baseline, Methods, and a summary of experiments. I need to keep my token usage efficient, and I’ll plan out the required actions carefully to avoid exceeding concurrency limits. Here are the planned actions:\n\n- /execute_action{review 588}\n- /execute_action{review 582}\n- /execute_action{review 569}\n- /execute_action{review 570}\n- /execute_action{review 574}\n- /execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/summary_scalaramp_loss_arch.csv}\n- /execute_action{storage write ariadne/reports/stagnation_report_draft.md}"
