- text: "All Idea 4 runs finished; result: no gain at H=128 or H=160. I’ll log these outcomes and finalize the Stagnation Protocol report draft. No new experiments for now.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/summary_scalaramp_loss_arch.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,cfg,p,H,learn_gamma,loss,extras,score,val_mae_1,val_mae_4,val_mae_8,val_mae_16,val_mae_32,decision\n  565,\"ScalarRamp baseline\",36,128,False,\"MAE+curv\",\"\", -0.026387,0.0195,0.0230,0.0255,0.0274,0.0284,baseline\n  567,\"ScalarRamp+Huber δ=0.01\",36,128,False,\"Huber+curv\",\"δ=0.01\", -0.026347,0.0195,0.0229,0.0255,0.0273,0.0282,accepted(H=128,min-setting)\n  569,\"ScalarRamp+Huber δ=0.02\",36,128,False,\"Huber+curv\",\"δ=0.02\", -0.026389,0.0195,0.0229,0.0256,0.0274,0.0283,rejected\n  570,\"ScalarRamp+Huber δ=0.03\",36,128,False,\"Huber+curv\",\"δ=0.03\", -0.026358,0.0195,0.0229,0.0255,0.0273,0.0283,positive-not-chosen\n  574,\"ScalarRamp+VarWeighted α=0.25\",36,128,False,\"VarianceWeighted+curv\"\
    ,\"α=0.25\", -0.026397,0.0195,0.0229,0.0255,0.0273,0.0281,rejected\n  579,\"ScalarRamp+PopMean λ=1e-3\",36,128,False,\"MAE+curv+popmean\",\"λ=1e-3\", -0.026316,0.0195,0.0229,0.0255,0.0273,0.0281,accepted(H=128)\n  588,\"ScalarRamp+PopMean λ=2e-3\",36,128,False,\"MAE+curv+popmean\",\"λ=2e-3\", -0.026379,0.0194,0.0229,0.0255,0.0273,0.0284,rejected\n  576,\"ScalarRamp+Huber δ=0.01\",36,160,False,\"Huber+curv\",\"δ=0.01\", -0.026253,0.0194,0.0229,0.0255,0.0272,0.0281,marginal(H=160)\n  582,\"ScalarRamp+PopMean λ=1e-3\",36,160,False,\"MAE+curv+popmean\",\"λ=1e-3\", -0.026293,0.0194,0.0229,0.0254,0.0272,0.0282,rejected\n  580,\"LearnGamma+Huber δ=0.01\",36,160,True,\"Huber+curv\",\"δ=0.01\", -0.026235,0.0197,0.0229,0.0254,0.0272,0.0280,rejected\n  584,\"LearnGamma+PopMean λ=1e-3\",36,160,True,\"MAE+curv+popmean\",\"λ=1e-3\", -0.026455,0.0197,0.0230,0.0256,0.0275,0.0282,rejected\n  592,\"ScalarRamp+HorizonBiasHead\",36,128,False,\"MAE+curv+32bias\",\"bias_scale=0.02,l2=5e-5,center=1e-3\", -0.026421,0.0195,0.0229,0.0256,0.0274,0.0283,rejected\n\
    \  593,\"ScalarRamp+HorizonBiasHead\",36,160,False,\"MAE+curv+32bias\",\"bias_scale=0.02,l2=5e-5,center=1e-3\", -0.026379,0.0195,0.0230,0.0256,0.0274,0.0281,rejected\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write ariadne/reports/stagnation_report_draft.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Stagnation Protocol I: Loss Probes and Minimal Calibration on ScalarRamp\n\n  Goal\n  - Follow the Architect’s protocol during stagnation: pick a simple baseline, generate three new ideas, test them in isolation, then attempt synthesis with the stronger backbone. Report results whether positive or negative.\n\n  Baseline\n  - Fourier LN ScalarRamp (p=36), H=128, MAE + curvature(λ=1e-4), lr=9e-4, clip=1.0, drop=0.05. Repro: −0.026387 (ID 565).\n\n  Ideas (single-variable changes; 3 seeds each; accept if gain ≥2e−5 with no early-step harm >5e−5)\n  1) Huber(δ) + curvature\n     - H=128: δ=0.01 → −0.026347 (ID 567, +4.0e−5, accepted); δ=0.02 → −0.026389 (ID 569, rejected); δ=0.03 → −0.026358 (ID 570, +2.9e−5, not chosen).\n\
    \     - H=160 confirm: δ=0.01 → −0.026253 (ID 576, +1.6e−5 vs −0.026269 ref), marginal (below threshold).\n     - Learnable-γ synthesis: −0.026235 (ID 580), negative vs SOTA line.\n\n  2) Variance-weighted horizon MAE (stop-grad), α=0.25 + curvature\n     - H=128: −0.026397 (ID 574), rejected.\n\n  3) Population-mean alignment penalty (λ_pop) + MAE + curvature\n     - H=128: λ=1e−3 → −0.026316 (ID 579, +7.1e−5, accepted); λ=2e−3 → −0.026379 (ID 588), rejected.\n     - H=160 confirm: λ=1e−3 → −0.026293 (ID 582), negative.\n     - Learnable-γ synthesis: −0.026455 (ID 584), negative.\n\n  Minimal Architecture Probe (orthogonal, bounded complexity)\n  - Add 32-scalar horizon bias head (global per-horizon offset), with small scale and L2/centering reg.\n  - H=128: −0.026421 (ID 592), rejected; H=160: −0.026379 (ID 593), rejected.\n\n  Metrics and Logs\n  - Early/late step MAEs and full table at: ariadne/analyses/summary_scalaramp_loss_arch.csv\n  - Three-seed means, automatic early stopping;\
    \ no custom training loops.\n\n  Insights\n  - On the simple ScalarRamp baseline (H=128), two loss-level nudges give small but consistent gains: Huber(δ=0.01) and λ_pop=1e−3. However, these effects (a) don’t scale with capacity (H=160) and (b) don’t transfer to the learnable-γ backbone, suggesting they correct minor biases that are already mitigated or overshadowed when the model can adapt horizon weighting.\n  - Variance-weighting by dispersion did not help, implying per-batch horizon difficulty adaptation is not the missing ingredient at this capacity.\n  - A minimal per-horizon calibration head (32 scalars) did not help, indicating simple global offsets are not the limiter.\n\n  Conclusion\n  - The simple baseline benefits from small robustification/mean-alignment tweaks; these do not generalize to stronger backbones. The limiting factor appears not to be the loss or per-horizon bias but capacity/representation for temporal dynamics (handled by learnable γ) and/or neuron-structure\
    \ modeling (still mostly ignored).\n  \n  Next Steps (post-stagnation write-up)\n  - Prepare paper for Archive (after maturity), including per-seed stats and ablations; position as negative/qualified results that narrow the search space.\n  - Future exploration (outside this protocol): consider parsimonious neuron-structure priors (e.g., low-rank temporal filters tied across neuron groups) or lightweight temporal state updates, but only with clean ablations.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Understanding Archive Access**


  I’m preparing to write a paper summarizing three tested ideas. However, it seems like I''m not mature enough to access the Archive Room yet, since I’m below the maturity limit of 50 ticks. For now, I can draft the paper in my private memory or storage, and access Public Memory in a read-only format. I need to finalize the stagnation report with negative results and update the summary CSV with results from Idea 4 before I can publish in the Archive later.**Assessing Next Steps**


  Our concurrency limit is free now, so we might want to move ahead with the Synthesis step 5, but the initial attempt with advanced baselines returned negative results. It seems wise to pause experiments and focus on writing the report, finalizing the private memory capsule. I could also reflect on new directions, like pivoting from a loss-level approach to exploring architecture-level options, perhaps through horizon-wise gating derived from input features, or using neuron grouping via k-means clusters. However, we need to prioritize exploring new baselines instead of focusing solely on state-of-the-art results.**Preparing to Write the Paper**


  I’m thinking that additional experiments may not be necessary right now since the protocol step 6 suggests writing a paper summarizing the three ideas we worked on, including an architecture test. It feels appropriate to draft the paper and save it to storage along with important details like research contributions, evaluation ID tables, methods, ablation details, and insights, including acceptance criteria and negative results. I should also update the summary CSV to add Idea 4 results marked as "rejected," and append the new rows for 592 and 593 before saving it again.**Generating and Updating Files**


  I''m planning to generate the file content again with the complete set of data. I can also utilize the Private Memory Room to create a new capsule for the "Stagnation Protocol I: Results." Since Private Memory is for my records, updating the "stagnation_report_draft.md" in storage seems appropriate. I’ll adhere to the concurrency limit of ≤2, avoiding new experiments to keep things efficient. I’ll include needed YAML blocks while ensuring our responses are concise. My actions will consist of updating the summary CSV with Idea 4 results and revising the stagnation report with minimal horizon-bias results and next steps.**Finalizing Contributions and Conclusions**


  I’m focusing on creating a summary of contributions and concluding the report. I might create a private memory capsule or reply to an existing one, but I won’t go to the Archive yet since I’m still immature. I’ll propose writing to storage for the CSV and the stagnation report draft. I will append lines 592 and 593 to the CSV for Idea 4 results, noting their scores and early step values. The stagnation report will include sections on the minimal architecture and a conclusion. I’ll include necessary YAML commands and keep in mind there won''t be any new submissions. Let''s get this done!'
