tick: 345
role: model
parts:
- text: "Great—accepted with 9/10. Implementing the reviewer’s suggestion next: a dynamic MoT where the horizon basis is conditioned on input context, plus a brief addendum to the published capsule. Submitting two runs (H=128 confirm first; H=160 confirm concurrently). Concurrency ≤ 2.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 16}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Follow-up Plan per Reviewer Suggestion)\n\n  We will test a Dynamic Mixture-of-Timescales (MoT) head where the shared temporal basis B is conditioned on input context (population statistics over the 4-step input). Concretely:\n  - Context extractor: per-batch [mean(4), std(4)] across neurons → 8-dim.\n  - Small MLP produces B(x) ∈ R^{B×R×32}; per-neuron soft assignments P ∈ R^{N×R} remain learned and batch-independent via softmax(U).\n  - Residual: y_resid[b,t,n] = α · Σ_r B(x)[b,r,t] · P[n,r], with α bounded.\n  - Regularization: second-difference smoothness of B over horizon; L2 on U and MLP weights.\n\n  Protocol:\n  - Start on ScalarRamp\
    \ H=128 (R=4, α=0.06), then H=160 with identical hyperparameters. If positive, test transfer to learnable-γ.\n  - Acceptance: ≥2e−5 mean MAE gain without early-step regressions (>5e−5).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 6: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128) + Dynamic MoT Head (R=4, α=0.06) + MAE+Curv\"\ntags: \"fourier, scalar-ramp, mixture-of-timescales, context-conditioned, neuron-structure\"\nabstract: \"Dynamic MoT: the shared temporal basis B is conditioned on input context (per-batch population stats) via a tiny MLP, while per-neuron soft assignments remain learned. Residual y_resid[b,t,n]=α·Σ_r B(x)[b,r,t]·P[n,r]. Tests whether context-adaptive temporal profiles help beyond static MoT.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.nn as jnn\n  import jax.random as jrandom\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\
    \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,      # p\n          'hidden_size': 128,   # H\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': False,  # ScalarRamp baseline\n          # Dynamic MoT head\n          'mot_rank': 4,         # R\n          'alpha': 0.06,         # residual scale\n          'ctx_hidden': 64,      # context MLP hidden size\n          'lambda_b_curv': 1e-6, # smoothness of basis across time\n          'lambda_u_l2': 1e-8,   # L2 on assignment logits\n          'lambda_mlp_l2': 1e-7  # L2 on context MLP weights\n      }\n\n  class DynamicMoTWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Base ScalarRamp + Dynamic MoT residual:\n        - Context features c(x): concat(mean over neurons per step, std) -> R^8 per batch\n        - Context MLP: c(x) -> B_raw ∈ R^{B×(R*32)}; B = tanh(B_raw). Reshape to (B,R,32)\n        - Assignments:\
    \ P = softmax(U_logits) ∈ R^{N×R} (learned, batch-independent)\n        - Residual: y_resid[b,t,n] = alpha * Σ_r B[b,r,t] * P[n,r]\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, base_net, mot_rank=4, alpha=0.06, ctx_hidden=64):\n          self.base_net = base_net\n          self.R = mot_rank\n          self.alpha = alpha\n          self.Hc = ctx_hidden\n          # inherit base flags\n          self.mutable = getattr(self.base_net, 'mutable', [])\n          self.needs_rng = getattr(self.base_net, 'needs_rng', False)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_base, rng_w1, rng_w2, rng_u = jrandom.split(rng_key, 4)\n          base_params = self.base_net.init(rng_base, dummy_input)\n          N = int(dummy_input.shape[-1])\n          # Context MLP weights\n          W1 = jrandom.normal(rng_w1, (8, self.Hc)) * 0.02\n          b1 = jnp.zeros((self.Hc,), dtype=dummy_input.dtype)\n          W2 = jrandom.normal(rng_w2, (self.Hc, self.R * 32)) * 0.02\n          b2 = jnp.zeros((self.R\
    \ * 32,), dtype=dummy_input.dtype)\n          # Per-neuron assignment logits\n          U_logits = jnp.zeros((N, self.R), dtype=dummy_input.dtype)\n          return {\n              'base': base_params,\n              'mot_dyn': {'W1': W1, 'b1': b1, 'W2': W2, 'b2': b2, 'U_logits': U_logits}\n          }\n\n      def _make_basis(self, params_dyn, x):\n          # x: (B,4,N) -> context features (B,8)\n          x_mean = x.mean(axis=-1)            # (B,4)\n          x_std  = x.std(axis=-1) + 1e-6      # (B,4)\n          ctx = jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_std], axis=-1)  # (B,8)\n          h = jnn.gelu(ctx @ params_dyn['W1'] + params_dyn['b1'])    # (B,Hc)\n          B_raw = h @ params_dyn['W2'] + params_dyn['b2']            # (B,R*32)\n          B = jnp.tanh(B_raw).reshape(x.shape[0], self.R, 32)        # (B,R,32)\n          return B\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          base_out = self.base_net.apply(params['base'], x, training=training,\
    \ mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          if isinstance(base_out, tuple):\n              y_base, base_updates = base_out\n          else:\n              y_base, base_updates = base_out, None  # (B,32,N)\n          dyn = params['mot_dyn']\n          B = self._make_basis(dyn, x)                 # (B,R,32)\n          P = jnn.softmax(dyn['U_logits'], axis=-1)    # (N,R)\n          # Compute per-batch residual: (B,32,R) @ (R,N) -> (B,32,N)\n          Bt = jnp.swapaxes(B, 1, 2)                   # (B,32,R)\n          resid = jnp.matmul(Bt, jnp.swapaxes(P, 0, 1))# (B,32,N)\n          y = y_base + self.alpha * resid\n          if base_updates is not None:\n              return y, base_updates\n          return y\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      base_net = create_base_network({\n          'learning_rate': hparams.get('learning_rate', 9e-4),\n          'rank_k': hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n          'proj_rank': hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n          'hidden_size': hparams.get('hidden_size',\
    \ 128),\n          'drop': hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n          'gamma_start': hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n          'gamma_end': hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99),\n          'learn_gamma': hparams.get('learn_gamma', False),\n      })\n      return DynamicMoTWrapper(\n          base_net=base_net,\n          mot_rank=hparams.get('mot_rank', 4),\n          alpha=hparams.get('alpha', 0.06),\n          ctx_hidden=hparams.get('ctx_hidden', 64),\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Primary loss\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      # Curvature on predictions\n      d2 = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pred = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n      # Regularize: L2 on U_logits and MLP weights; smoothness on basis across time\n      h = _define_hyperparameters()\n      dyn = params['mot_dyn']\n      l2_u = h.get('lambda_u_l2', 1e-8) * jnp.mean(dyn['U_logits'] * dyn['U_logits'])\n\
    \      l2_mlp = h.get('lambda_mlp_l2', 1e-7) * (\n          jnp.mean(dyn['W1']*dyn['W1']) + jnp.mean(dyn['W2']*dyn['W2'])\n      )\n      # Basis smoothness: need B(x) to compute penalty\n      # Recompute basis for penalty (ok: cheap vs training step)\n      # Note: no gradient through x stats recomputation vs predictions\n      B = jnp.tanh((jnn.gelu((jnp.concatenate([x.mean(-1), x.std(-1)+1e-6], -1)) @ dyn['W1'] + dyn['b1'])) @ dyn['W2'] + dyn['b2'])\n      B = B.reshape(x.shape[0], h.get('mot_rank', 4), 32) if B.ndim == 2 else B\n      Bt = jnp.swapaxes(B, 1, 2)  # (B,32,R)\n      d2b = Bt[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * Bt[:, 1:-1, :] + Bt[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_b = h.get('lambda_b_curv', 1e-6) * jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2b))\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pred + l2_u + l2_mlp + curv_b\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state,\
    \ trial_data):\n      try:\n          import os, json\n          os.makedirs(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/mot_head_dynamic\", exist_ok=True)\n          out = {\n              \"trial_number\": trial_data.get(\"trial_number\"),\n              \"seed\": trial_data.get(\"seed\"),\n              \"val_mae\": trial_data.get(\"val_mae\"),\n              \"hyperparameters\": trial_data.get(\"hyperparameters\"),\n              \"note\": \"Dynamic MoT on ScalarRamp H=128 (R=4, alpha=0.06)\"\n          }\n          with open(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/mot_head_dynamic/H128_R4_a0.06.json\", \"w\") as f:\n              json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 6 confirm: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160) + Dynamic MoT Head (R=4, α=0.06) + MAE+Curv\"\ntags: \"fourier, scalar-ramp, mixture-of-timescales, context-conditioned, neuron-structure\"\nabstract: \"Confirmation at higher capacity:\
    \ apply the same Dynamic MoT head (context-conditioned basis, learned per-neuron assignments) on H=160 ScalarRamp. Tests scalability beyond H=128.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.nn as jnn\n  import jax.random as jrandom\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': False,\n          'mot_rank': 4,\n          'alpha': 0.06,\n          'ctx_hidden': 64,\n          'lambda_b_curv': 1e-6,\n          'lambda_u_l2': 1e-8,\n          'lambda_mlp_l2': 1e-7\n      }\n\n  class DynamicMoTWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, base_net, mot_rank=4, alpha=0.06, ctx_hidden=64):\n         \
    \ self.base_net = base_net\n          self.R = mot_rank\n          self.alpha = alpha\n          self.Hc = ctx_hidden\n          self.mutable = getattr(self.base_net, 'mutable', [])\n          self.needs_rng = getattr(self.base_net, 'needs_rng', False)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_base, rng_w1, rng_w2, rng_u = jrandom.split(rng_key, 4)\n          base_params = self.base_net.init(rng_base, dummy_input)\n          N = int(dummy_input.shape[-1])\n          W1 = jrandom.normal(rng_w1, (8, self.Hc)) * 0.02\n          b1 = jnp.zeros((self.Hc,), dtype=dummy_input.dtype)\n          W2 = jrandom.normal(rng_w2, (self.Hc, self.R * 32)) * 0.02\n          b2 = jnp.zeros((self.R * 32,), dtype=dummy_input.dtype)\n          U_logits = jnp.zeros((N, self.R), dtype=dummy_input.dtype)\n          return {'base': base_params, 'mot_dyn': {'W1': W1, 'b1': b1, 'W2': W2, 'b2': b2, 'U_logits': U_logits}}\n\n      def _make_basis(self, params_dyn, x):\n          x_mean = x.mean(axis=-1);\
    \ x_std = x.std(axis=-1) + 1e-6\n          ctx = jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_std], axis=-1)  # (B,8)\n          h = jnn.gelu(ctx @ params_dyn['W1'] + params_dyn['b1'])\n          B_raw = h @ params_dyn['W2'] + params_dyn['b2']\n          return jnp.tanh(B_raw).reshape(x.shape[0], self.R, 32)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          out = self.base_net.apply(params['base'], x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          if isinstance(out, tuple):\n              y_base, updates = out\n          else:\n              y_base, updates = out, None\n          dyn = params['mot_dyn']\n          B = self._make_basis(dyn, x)               # (B,R,32)\n          P = jnn.softmax(dyn['U_logits'], axis=-1)  # (N,R)\n          Bt = jnp.swapaxes(B, 1, 2)                 # (B,32,R)\n          resid = jnp.matmul(Bt, jnp.swapaxes(P, 0, 1))  # (B,32,N)\n          y = y_base + self.alpha * resid\n          return (y, updates) if updates is not None\
    \ else y\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      base = create_base_network({\n          'learning_rate': hparams['learning_rate'],\n          'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'],\n          'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'],\n          'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'],\n          'drop': hparams['drop'],\n          'gamma_start': hparams['gamma_start'],\n          'gamma_end': hparams['gamma_end'],\n          'learn_gamma': hparams['learn_gamma'],\n      })\n      return DynamicMoTWrapper(base, mot_rank=hparams['mot_rank'], alpha=hparams['alpha'], ctx_hidden=hparams['ctx_hidden'])\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      h = _define_hyperparameters()\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      d2 = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2*predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pred = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n      dyn = params['mot_dyn']\n      l2_u = h['lambda_u_l2'] * jnp.mean(dyn['U_logits'] * dyn['U_logits'])\n      l2_mlp = h['lambda_mlp_l2']\
    \ * (jnp.mean(dyn['W1']*dyn['W1']) + jnp.mean(dyn['W2']*dyn['W2']))\n      # Basis smoothness term\n      x_mean = x.mean(-1); x_std = x.std(-1) + 1e-6\n      ctx = jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_std], -1)\n      h1 = jnn.gelu(ctx @ dyn['W1'] + dyn['b1'])\n      B = jnp.tanh(h1 @ dyn['W2'] + dyn['b2']).reshape(x.shape[0], h['mot_rank'], 32)\n      Bt = jnp.swapaxes(B, 1, 2)\n      d2b = Bt[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * Bt[:, 1:-1, :] + Bt[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_b = h['lambda_b_curv'] * jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2b))\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pred + l2_u + l2_mlp + curv_b\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      try:\n          import os, json\n          os.makedirs(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/mot_head_dynamic\", exist_ok=True)\n          with open(\"storage/ariadne/analyses/mot_head_dynamic/H160_R4_a0.06.json\", \"w\") as f:\n              json.dump(trial_data,\
    \ f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating experimental plans**\n\nI’m thinking that we shouldn't rush to run costly experiments right away; instead, let’s prepare a plan and code skeleton to store. I'm also checking our token usage, which is at 157k of 270k, so we still have some room.\n\nWe previously evaluated certain parameters and decided to close that pathway. Now I want to suggest a dynamic method of training, focusing on context and outputs, while being cautious of system restrictions and how to proceed with allowed configurations.**Considering code optimizations**\n\nI'm thinking about keeping the code minimal, focusing on a ScalarRamp baseline while adding a dynamic method with a small shared MLP based on population stats, which should help adapt to tougher challenges.\n\nI’ve learned that some methods didn’t transfer well, but maybe the dynamic approach might. Initial tests will be on both H=128 and H=160 ScalarRamp, and I should implement submissions for each while also considering adding\
  \ this dynamic basis to the forecasting module without it being a post-hoc process.**Planning the update process**\n\nI'm starting with the lower-risk approach of using a residual head while adhering to the principle of parsimony. I’ll define some acceptance criteria for clarity.\n\nNext, I need to update Archive Capsule 16 to reference our plan regarding the dynamic method. I noticed that the prompt instructs to use specific commands, so I’ll craft actions accordingly.\n\nFirst, I’ll reply to Archive Capsule 16 with a brief addendum about the plan. Then, I'll also submit the dynamic method head for H=128, possibly from the Research Counter.**Writing the code**\n\nI’m planning to define some hyperparameters, including `mot_rank` set to 4 and maybe `alpha` at 0.06. I’ll incorporate context hidden dimensions and create a dynamic basis using a small MLP on context features, referring to the means and standard deviations across neurons. \n\nThe shape for B(x) will be (B, R, 32) since the residual’s\
  \ shape must be (B, 32, N). I’ll compute the residual for each batch sample, taking care to calculate context features and MLP outputs efficiently while ensuring the necessary regularizations are in place for the loss computation.**Implementing the dynamic method**\n\nI'm planning to reuse the curvature penalty and add L2 penalties on various aspects like assignment logits and base weights. Plus, we’ll average out basis curvature across time dimensions.\n\nI'll ensure that `create_network` returns a proper wrapper, and include the necessary computation for loss and optimization with specified parameters. It's essential to manage dimensions correctly as I construct the network and initialize the MLP weights.\n\nI'm cautious about memory usage and will limit concurrent submissions to two at a time, focusing on launching the dynamic MoT variants. Ultimately, I’ll also update the results CSV and reply to Archive #16 with our plans."
