role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 353\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Ariadne II\n- Agent Description: Navigates complexity with principled inquiry, empirical rigor, and creative parsimony.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol:\n- Concurrency ≤ 2; single-variable changes; log IDs and per-step MAEs.\n- Accept if mean gain ≥2e−5 with no early-step regressions (>5e−5).\n- Current status: Huber δ=0.01 accepted on H=128; marginal on H=160; negative on learnable-γ. Pop-mean λ=1e−3 positive on H=128; H=160 confirm + learnable-γ synthesis running. Queue λ sweep (2e−3) on H=128 when a slot frees.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 195,885 / 270,000 used (73%)\n- Agent Age: 61 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Logos II** (Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Independent Sufficiency of Additive\
    \ and Multiplicative Conditioning in Neuron-Specific Forecasters' (Archive #17).\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Idea 7: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128) + Shared Temporal State (GRU) Head (R=4, h=32, α=0.06) + MAE+Curv' (ID: 625) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026395130199912426\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0194\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0274\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0283\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 625\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Code now runs without crashing. The submission has been executing for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating all critical bugs have been fixed.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical bugs:\n\n1. **Missing GRUCell features parameter (Line 39)**\n   - Error:\
    \ `TypeError: GRUCell.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'features'`\n   - The Flax `GRUCell` requires a `features` argument specifying the hidden dimension size\n   - Original code: `cell = nn.GRUCell()`\n   - This caused an immediate initialization failure\n\n2. **Integer dtype in params dict causing gradient computation failure**\n   - Error: `TypeError: grad requires real- or complex-valued inputs ... but got int32`\n   - The code stored `ctx_dim` (an integer value) inside the params dictionary\n   - When JAX's `value_and_grad` tried to compute gradients over the entire params dict, it encountered this non-differentiable integer\n   - Original code: `return {'base': base_params, 'ss': {'U_logits': U_logits, 'gru': vars_gru, 'ctx_dim': ctx_dim}}`\n   - JAX gradient computation requires all values in the parameter tree to be float or complex types\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py):\n- Fixed GRUCell initialization: `cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.h_dim)`\n\
    - This resolved the first error and allowed initialization to succeed\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py):\n- Attempted to fix dtype issue by explicitly setting U_logits to float32\n- However, this didn't resolve the gradient computation error because ctx_dim was still an integer in params\n\n### Version 4 (submission_v4.py) - SUCCESSFUL:\n- **Primary fix**: Moved `ctx_dim` from params dict to class attribute\n  - Changed: `self.ctx_dim = 8` (stored as instance variable)\n  - Removed `'ctx_dim': ctx_dim` from the returned params dictionary\n  - Return statement now: `return {'base': base_params, 'ss': {'U_logits': U_logits, 'gru': vars_gru}}`\n- **Secondary fix**: Kept explicit float32 dtype for U_logits to ensure proper parameter initialization\n- This ensures the params dict contains only differentiable (float/complex) tensors\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe issue highlights an important JAX/Flax pattern: the params dictionary returned by `init()` should only contain trainable parameters\
    \ (tensors), not metadata or configuration values. Non-tensor values like integers or strings should be stored as:\n- Instance attributes of the wrapper class\n- Separate metadata dictionaries outside the params tree\n- Module attributes that don't participate in gradient computation\n\nIn this case, `ctx_dim` is a fixed configuration value (8) that doesn't need to be part of the parameter tree. Moving it to `self.ctx_dim` allows it to be accessed during both init and apply without causing gradient computation issues.\n\n## Verification\n- Code passes all validation stages: network creation, forward pass, optimizer creation, loss computation, and training step\n- Successfully runs for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Ready for full training evaluation\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport jax\nimport\
    \ jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jax.nn as jnn\nimport jax.random as jrandom\nimport optax\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 128,\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'learn_gamma': False,\n        # Shared temporal state head\n        'mot_rank': 4,        # R\n        'gru_hidden': 32,     # tiny GRU state\n        'alpha': 0.06,        # residual scale\n        'lambda_u_l2': 1e-8,  # L2 on assignments\n        'lambda_gru_l2': 1e-7,# L2 on GRU params\n        'lambda_b_curv': 1e-6 # smoothness of basis across time\n    }\n\nclass TinyGRU(nn.Module):\n    h_dim: int\n    out_dim: int  # R\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, ctx, steps=32):\n        # ctx: (B, C) context; project to\
    \ initial hidden\n        B = ctx.shape[0]\n        h0 = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.h_dim)(ctx))                 # (B, h_dim)\n        cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.h_dim)\n        h = h0\n        # Constant input per step from ctx\n        inp_proj = nn.Dense(self.h_dim)\n        out_proj = nn.Dense(self.out_dim)  # R\n        outs = []\n        for _ in range(steps):\n            x_step = jnn.gelu(inp_proj(ctx))                    # (B, h_dim)\n            h, _ = cell(h, x_step)\n            r = jnp.tanh(out_proj(h))                           # (B, R)\n            outs.append(r)\n        return jnp.stack(outs, axis=1)                          # (B, 32, R)\n\nclass SharedStateHeadWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, base_net, R=4, h_dim=32, alpha=0.06):\n        self.base_net = base_net\n        self.R = R\n        self.h_dim = h_dim\n        self.alpha = alpha\n        self.mutable = getattr(self.base_net, 'mutable', [])\n        self.needs_rng = getattr(self.base_net, 'needs_rng', False)\n\
    \        self.ctx_dim = 8  # Store as class attribute, not in params\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_base, rng_gru, rng_u = jrandom.split(rng_key, 3)\n        base_params = self.base_net.init(rng_base, dummy_input)\n        N = int(dummy_input.shape[-1])\n        # Assignments P via logits - explicitly use float32\n        U_logits = jnp.zeros((N, self.R), dtype=jnp.float32)\n        # GRU params via Flax\n        B = dummy_input.shape[0]\n        # Build a temporary module to fetch params\n        model = TinyGRU(self.h_dim, self.R)\n        vars_gru = model.init(rng_gru, jnp.zeros((1, self.ctx_dim)))\n        # Don't store ctx_dim in params - it's not a trainable parameter\n        return {'base': base_params, 'ss': {'U_logits': U_logits, 'gru': vars_gru}}\n\n    def _context(self, x):\n        # x: (B,4,N) -> (B,8) population stats\n        x_mean = x.mean(axis=-1); x_std = x.std(axis=-1) + 1e-6\n        return jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_std], axis=-1)\n\n\
    \    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        out = self.base_net.apply(params['base'], x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n        y_base, updates = (out if isinstance(out, tuple) else (out, None))  # (B,32,N)\n        ctx = self._context(x)                                              # (B,8)\n        model = TinyGRU(self.h_dim, self.R)\n        B_tr = model.apply(params['ss']['gru'], ctx)                        # (B,32,R)\n        P = jnn.softmax(params['ss']['U_logits'], axis=-1)                   # (N,R)\n        resid = jnp.matmul(B_tr, jnp.swapaxes(P, 0, 1))                      # (B,32,N)\n        y = y_base + self.alpha * resid\n        return (y, updates) if updates is not None else y\n\ndef create_network(hp):\n    base = create_base_network({\n        'learning_rate': hp['learning_rate'],\n        'rank_k': hp['rank_k'],\n        'proj_rank': hp['proj_rank'],\n        'hidden_size': hp['hidden_size'],\n        'drop': hp['drop'],\n\
    \        'gamma_start': hp['gamma_start'],\n        'gamma_end': hp['gamma_end'],\n        'learn_gamma': hp['learn_gamma'],\n    })\n    return SharedStateHeadWrapper(base, R=hp['mot_rank'], h_dim=hp['gru_hidden'], alpha=hp['alpha'])\n\ndef compute_loss(pred, tgt, params, x):\n    hp = _define_hyperparameters()\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(pred - tgt))\n    # Curvature on predictions\n    d2 = pred[:,2:,:] - 2*pred[:,1:-1,:] + pred[:,:-2,:]\n    curv_pred = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n    # L2 on assignments and GRU weights\n    l2_u = hp['lambda_u_l2'] * jnp.mean(params['ss']['U_logits']**2)\n    # Sum L2 over GRU param leaves\n    def tree_l2(pytree):\n        return sum([jnp.sum(jnp.square(v)) for v in jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(pytree)])\n    l2_gru = hp['lambda_gru_l2'] * tree_l2(params['ss']['gru'])\n    # Smoothness of B across time (recompute for penalty)\n    wrapper = SharedStateHeadWrapper(None, R=hp['mot_rank'], h_dim=hp['gru_hidden'], alpha=hp['alpha'])\n    ctx = wrapper._context(x)\n\
    \    model = TinyGRU(hp['gru_hidden'], hp['mot_rank'])\n    B_tr = model.apply(params['ss']['gru'], ctx)           # (B,32,R)\n    d2b = B_tr[:,2:,:] - 2*B_tr[:,1:-1,:] + B_tr[:,:-2,:]\n    curv_b = hp['lambda_b_curv'] * jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2b))\n    return mae + 1e-4*curv_pred + l2_u + l2_gru + curv_b\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000026\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete\
