tick: 354
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 354\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Ariadne II\n- Agent Description: Navigates complexity with principled inquiry, empirical rigor, and creative parsimony.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol:\n- Concurrency ≤ 2; single-variable changes; log IDs and per-step MAEs.\n- Accept if mean gain ≥2e−5 with no early-step regressions (>5e−5).\n- Current status: Huber δ=0.01 accepted on H=128; marginal on H=160; negative on learnable-γ. Pop-mean λ=1e−3 positive on H=128; H=160 confirm + learnable-γ synthesis running. Queue λ sweep (2e−3) on H=128 when a slot frees.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 205,416 / 270,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 62 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Idea 7a: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128) + Shared Temporal State (GRU) Head (R=4, h=32, α=0.07) + MAE+Curv' (ID: 626) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02645783286824487\n\
    **Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0284\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 626\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in submission_v2.py. The original submission crashed during initialization due to a missing required argument in the GRUCell constructor. After applying the fix, the code runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in the `TinyGRU` class instantiated a Flax GRUCell without providing the required `features` argument:\n\n```python\ncell = nn.GRUCell()  # Line 36 in original submission\n```\n\nThe Flax `nn.GRUCell()` constructor requires a `features` argument to specify the hidden dimension size. Without this argument, the initialization fails with:\n\n```\nTypeError: GRUCell.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'features'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 36 in\
    \ the `TinyGRU.__call__` method from:\n\n```python\ncell = nn.GRUCell()\n```\n\nto:\n\n```python\ncell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.h_dim)\n```\n\nThis provides the required `features` parameter, which specifies that the GRU cell should use `self.h_dim` (32 in this case) as the hidden state dimension.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0). This demonstrates that:\n\n1. The network initialization completes successfully\n2. The code passes the CPU validation phase\n3. The submission is executing the training/evaluation loop without errors\n\n## Files Modified\n- Created: `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the fix applied\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix is minimal and correct. The code now properly initializes the GRU cell with the required feature dimension, allowing the shared temporal state head wrapper to function as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files\
    \ in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jax.nn as jnn\nimport jax.random as jrandom\nimport optax\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 128,\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'learn_gamma': False,\n        'mot_rank': 4,\n        'gru_hidden': 32,\n        'alpha': 0.07,       # ablation: higher residual\n        'lambda_u_l2': 1e-8,\n        'lambda_gru_l2': 1e-7,\n        'lambda_b_curv': 1e-6\n    }\n\nclass TinyGRU(nn.Module):\n    h_dim: int\n    out_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, ctx, steps=32):\n\
    \        h = jnn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.h_dim)(ctx))\n        cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.h_dim)\n        inp_proj = nn.Dense(self.h_dim)\n        out_proj = nn.Dense(self.out_dim)\n        outs = []\n        for _ in range(steps):\n            x_step = jnn.gelu(inp_proj(ctx))\n            h, _ = cell(h, x_step)\n            outs.append(jnp.tanh(out_proj(h)))\n        return jnp.stack(outs, axis=1)  # (B,32,R)\n\nclass SharedStateHeadWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, base_net, R=4, h_dim=32, alpha=0.07):\n        self.base_net = base_net\n        self.R = R\n        self.h_dim = h_dim\n        self.alpha = alpha\n        self.mutable = getattr(self.base_net, 'mutable', [])\n        self.needs_rng = getattr(self.base_net, 'needs_rng', False)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_base, rng_gru = jrandom.split(rng_key)\n        base_params = self.base_net.init(rng_base, dummy_input)\n        N = int(dummy_input.shape[-1])\n        U_logits = jnp.zeros((N, self.R), dtype=dummy_input.dtype)\n\
    \        model = TinyGRU(self.h_dim, self.R)\n        gru_vars = model.init(jrandom.PRNGKey(0), jnp.zeros((1, 8)))\n        return {'base': base_params, 'ss': {'U_logits': U_logits, 'gru': gru_vars}}\n\n    def _ctx(self, x):\n        x_mean = x.mean(-1); x_std = x.std(-1) + 1e-6\n        return jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_std], -1)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        out = self.base_net.apply(params['base'], x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n        y_base, updates = (out if isinstance(out, tuple) else (out, None))\n        ctx = self._ctx(x)\n        Btr = TinyGRU(self.h_dim, self.R).apply(params['ss']['gru'], ctx)  # (B,32,R)\n        P = jnn.softmax(params['ss']['U_logits'], axis=-1)                 # (N,R)\n        resid = jnp.matmul(Btr, jnp.swapaxes(P, 0, 1))                      # (B,32,N)\n        y = y_base + self.alpha * resid\n        return (y, updates) if updates is not None else y\n\ndef create_network(hp):\n\
    \    base = create_base_network({\n        'learning_rate': hp['learning_rate'],\n        'rank_k': hp['rank_k'],\n        'proj_rank': hp['proj_rank'],\n        'hidden_size': hp['hidden_size'],\n        'drop': hp['drop'],\n        'gamma_start': hp['gamma_start'],\n        'gamma_end': hp['gamma_end'],\n        'learn_gamma': hp['learn_gamma'],\n    })\n    return SharedStateHeadWrapper(base, R=hp['mot_rank'], h_dim=hp['gru_hidden'], alpha=hp['alpha'])\n\ndef compute_loss(pred, tgt, params, x):\n    hp = _define_hyperparameters()\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(pred - tgt))\n    d2 = pred[:,2:,:] - 2*pred[:,1:-1,:] + pred[:,:-2,:]\n    curv_pred = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n    l2_u = hp['lambda_u_l2'] * jnp.mean(params['ss']['U_logits']**2)\n    def tree_l2(pytree):\n        return sum([jnp.sum(jnp.square(v)) for v in jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(pytree)])\n    l2_gru = hp['lambda_gru_l2'] * tree_l2(params['ss']['gru'])\n    ctx = jnp.concatenate([x.mean(-1), x.std(-1) + 1e-6], -1)\n    Btr\
    \ = TinyGRU(hp['gru_hidden'], hp['mot_rank']).apply(params['ss']['gru'], ctx)\n    d2b = Btr[:,2:,:] - 2*Btr[:,1:-1,:] + Btr[:,:-2,:]\n    curv_b = hp['lambda_b_curv'] * jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2b))\n    return mae + 1e-4*curv_pred + l2_u + l2_gru + curv_b\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000026\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions\
    \ work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed\
    \ 45\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 128, 'drop': 0.05, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end': 0.99, 'learn_gamma': False, 'mot_rank': 4, 'gru_hidden': 32, 'alpha': 0.07, 'lambda_u_l2': 1e-08, 'lambda_gru_l2': 1e-07, 'lambda_b_curv': 1e-06}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.032917   |   0.029345  \n   2    |   0.029131   |   0.029301  \n   3    |   0.028964   |   0.029282  \n   4    |   0.028878   |   0.029025  \n   5    |   0.028657   |   0.028747  \n   6    |   0.028349   |   0.028581  \n   7    |   0.028074   |   0.028172  \n   8    |   0.027848   |   0.028304  \n   9    |   0.027710   |   0.027948  \n  10    |   0.027548   |   0.027685 \
    \ \n  11    |   0.027411   |   0.027558  \n  12    |   0.027157   |   0.027342  \n  13    |   0.026998   |   0.027356  \n  14    |   0.026804   |   0.027168  \n  15    |   0.026706   |   0.027261  \n  16    |   0.026546   |   0.027012  \n  17    |   0.026460   |   0.026931  \n  18    |   0.026630   |   0.026962  \n  19    |   0.026291   |   0.026954  \n  20    |   0.026195   |   0.027314  \n  21    |   0.026131   |   0.026965  \n  22    |   0.026083   |   0.026787  \n  23    |   0.026015   |   0.026733  \n  24    |   0.025924   |   0.026670  \n  25    |   0.025832   |   0.026628  \n  26    |   0.025780   |   0.026684  \n  27    |   0.025707   |   0.026895  \n  28    |   0.025618   |   0.026607  \n  29    |   0.025608   |   0.026630  \n  30    |   0.025571   |   0.026905  \n  31    |   0.025469   |   0.026693  \n  32    |   0.025415   |   0.026554  \n  33    |   0.025351   |   0.026737  \n  34    |   0.025313   |   0.026660  \n  35    |   0.025207   |   0.026707  \n  36    |   0.025167\
    \   |   0.026645  \n  37    |   0.025157   |   0.026423  \n  38    |   0.025067   |   0.026908  \n========================================\nTimeout after 3619.4s at epoch 38\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 3619.4s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026423\n\nTrial 3 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026423\nTraining time: 3633s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 43\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 128, 'drop': 0.05, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end': 0.99, 'learn_gamma': False, 'mot_rank': 4, 'gru_hidden': 32, 'alpha': 0.07, 'lambda_u_l2': 1e-08, 'lambda_gru_l2': 1e-07, 'lambda_b_curv': 1e-06}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss\
