role: model
parts:
- text: "Synthesis results logged; holding while H=160 confirmations run (IDs 636, 637). Updating analysis artifacts only; no new jobs to keep concurrency ≤2.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/mot_head/results_latest.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,cfg,p,H,learn_gamma,head,R,alpha,delta,score,val_mae_1,val_mae_4,val_mae_8,val_mae_16,val_mae_32,decision,notes\n  565,ScalarRamp baseline,36,128,False,None,0,0.00,, -0.026387,0.0195,0.0230,0.0255,0.0274,0.0284,baseline,Repro reference\n  602,ScalarRamp+MoT,36,128,False,MoT,4,0.07,, -0.026336,0.0195,0.0229,0.0255,0.0273,0.0282,accepted(+5.1e-5),Static MoT head\n  608,ScalarRamp+MoT,36,128,False,MoT,2,0.04,, -0.026354,0.0195,0.0230,0.0255,0.0273,0.0284,accepted(+3.3e-5),Smaller MoT head\n  631,Synthesis MoT+Huber,36,128,False,MoT,4,0.07,0.01, -0.026249,0.0194,0.0229,0.0254,0.0272,0.0281,accepted(+1.38e-4),No early-step harm\n  633,Synthesis MoT(2)+Huber,36,128,False,MoT,2,0.04,0.01, -0.026379,0.0195,0.0229,0.0254,0.0274,0.0284,rejected(<+1e-5),Below\
    \ threshold\n  636,Synthesis confirm,36,160,False,MoT,4,0.07,0.01, running,,,,,,pending,H=160 transfer check\n  637,Synthesis confirm v2,36,160,False,MoT,4,0.06,0.01, running,,,,,,pending,H=160 ablation (smaller α)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/mot_head/interpretation.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  MoT + Huber synthesis (H=128) — Interim Interpretation\n\n  Findings\n  - Static MoT head (R=4, α=0.07) alone improved baseline by ~5.1e−5; Huber(δ=0.01) alone improved by ~4.0e−5.\n  - Combined (ID 631), gains add superlinearly: +1.38e−4 vs baseline, with t1/t4 unchanged or slightly better.\n  - Smaller MoT (R=2, α=0.04) + Huber (ID 633) underperforms the larger MoT + Huber, suggesting capacity matters at H=128.\n\n  Hypothesis\n  - Huber reduces tail leverage; MoT provides structured horizon residuals across neuron groups. The two act on complementary failure modes on the simple baseline.\n  - Prior negatives on H=160 suggest stronger temporal capacity subsumes MoT’s\
    \ benefit; confirmations (IDs 636/637) will test if synthesis buckles similarly.\n\n  Next (after 636/637 finish)\n  - If both H=160 confirms are negative: document non-transfer; close MoT line and roll insights into addendum.\n  - If any is positive: run a second confirm with the same settings to solidify the result, then update summary CSV and consider a short archive note.\n```"
